","text":"*Elemental Tempo*: it acts twice a round."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–3 of its flavour."},{"name":"Signature Move","text":"*Signature Move*: its flavour's Adult move."}],"harvest":"An elemental core (an enchanting focus).","role":"Solo","wants":"As Juvenile, or whatever its summoner commands.","tactics":"Engulfs the toughest fighter, then surges at everyone else.","tell":"as Juvenile.","exploit":"as Juvenile. Breaking its summoner's control frees it, and a freed elemental often just leaves.","type":"Elemental","kind":"tier","family":"elemental","tier":"Adult","tierNumber":2,"order":196},{"id":"elder-elemental","name":"Elder Elemental","kr":120,"section":"Elementals","typeLine":"Elemental","tags":[],"description":"The size of a hill. Old ones of these get worshipped by people who don't know better.","hp":1100,"hpNote":null,"defence":5,"minHit":9,"speed":"40 ft, plus its flavour's movement","stats":{"str":2,"dex":5,"con":2,"int":8,"wis":6,"cha":7},"combat":{"melee":3,"ranged":null,"dodge":12,"disengage":10,"casting":4},"attacks":[{"name":"Multiattack","text":"Multiattack: Slam ×3, 2d20 each, +3d2 flavour status.","multiattack":true,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["2d20"],"status":[{"dice":"3d2","n":3,"status":"flavour status"}]},{"name":"Engulf","text":"*Engulf* (as Adult, 4d10 a turn, up to two creatures).","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":"as Adult, 4d10 a turn, up to two creatures","damage":["4d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Surge","text":"*Surge* (2-turn recharge): a 60 ft burst, 12d10, +5d2 flavour status. A Dodge roll halves the damage.","multiattack":false,"recharge":2,"limit":null,"damage":["12d10"],"status":[{"dice":"5d2","n":5,"status":"flavour status"}]}],"traits":[{"name":null,"text":"Everything the Adult has, plus:"},{"name":"Aura","text":"*Aura*: 3d6, 15 ft."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–5."},{"name":"Shatter","text":"*Shatter*: the first time it drops below half HP, it splits into two Adult Elementals of the same flavour, each at full HP."}],"harvest":"An elder core (legendary enchanting focus).","role":"Solo","wants":"Worship, or the balance of its element.","tactics":"Fights as one, then Shatters into two to split the party.","tell":"cracks of its element run across its body just before it Shatters.","exploit":"save your big damage until after it Shatters.","type":"Elemental","kind":"tier","family":"elemental","tier":"Elder","tierNumber":3,"order":197},{"id":"ancient-elemental","name":"Ancient Elemental","kr":225,"section":"Elementals","typeLine":"Elemental","tags":[],"description":"A walking storm, wildfire or landslide that can change the map.","hp":2200,"hpNote":null,"defence":6,"minHit":11,"speed":"50 ft, plus its flavour's movement","stats":{"str":1,"dex":4,"con":1,"int":5,"wis":4,"cha":5},"combat":{"melee":3,"ranged":null,"dodge":11,"disengage":9,"casting":2},"attacks":[{"name":"Multiattack","text":"Multiattack: Slam ×3, 3d20 each, +4d2 flavour status.","multiattack":true,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["3d20"],"status":[{"dice":"4d2","n":4,"status":"flavour status"}]},{"name":"Engulf","text":"*Engulf* (as Elder, 5d10 a turn).","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":"as Elder, 5d10 a turn","damage":["5d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Surge","text":"*Surge* (2-turn recharge): a 120 ft burst, 18d10, +7d2 flavour status. A Dodge roll halves the damage.","multiattack":false,"recharge":2,"limit":null,"damage":["18d10"],"status":[{"dice":"7d2","n":7,"status":"flavour status"}]}],"traits":[{"name":null,"text":"Everything the Elder has (but no Shatter), plus:"},{"name":"Aura","text":"*Aura*: 4d6, 30 ft."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–7."},{"name":"Ancient Tempo","text":"*Ancient Tempo*: it acts three times a round."},{"name":"Spawn","text":"*Spawn* (once per combat): 1d4 Juvenile Elementals of its flavour appear next to it."},{"name":"Signature Move","text":"*Signature Move*: its flavour's Ancient upgrade."}],"harvest":"An ancient core (legendary item core).","role":"Solo","wants":"To reshape the land in its image.","tactics":"It's a walking disaster. Spawn early, Surge often, and use its signature move to change the battlefield.","tell":"as Juvenile.","exploit":"weakness, and fighting it somewhere that isn't its element.","type":"Elemental","kind":"tier","family":"elemental","tier":"Ancient","tierNumber":4,"order":198},{"id":"primordial-elemental","name":"Primordial Elemental","kr":450,"section":"Elementals","typeLine":"Elemental","tags":[],"description":"The flavour itself, awake. Each one is unique: there is one of each flavour, at most.","hp":4500,"hpNote":null,"defence":7,"minHit":13,"speed":"60 ft, plus its flavour's movement","stats":{"str":1,"dex":2,"con":1,"int":2,"wis":2,"cha":3},"combat":{"melee":3,"ranged":null,"dodge":10,"disengage":8,"casting":1},"attacks":[{"name":"Multiattack","text":"Multiattack: Slam ×3, 2d50 each, +5d2 flavour status.","multiattack":true,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["2d50"],"status":[{"dice":"5d2","n":5,"status":"flavour status"}]},{"name":"Surge","text":"*Surge* (2-turn recharge): a 300 ft burst, 25d10, +10d2 flavour status. A Dodge roll halves the damage.","multiattack":false,"recharge":2,"limit":null,"damage":["25d10"],"status":[{"dice":"10d2","n":10,"status":"flavour status"}]}],"traits":[{"name":null,"text":"Everything the Ancient has, plus:"},{"name":"Aura","text":"*Aura*: 6d6, 60 ft."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–9."},{"name":"Living Domain","text":"*Living Domain*: the land within a mile becomes its flavour's lair."},{"name":"Undying","text":"*Undying*: it can't be destroyed, only sealed or sent back to its source. Sealing one is a quest in itself."}],"harvest":"None. It can only be sealed, and the seal is the prize.","role":"Set piece","wants":"Everything to return to its element.","tactics":"The fight is about holding it off long enough to complete the seal.","tell":"the world itself changes to its flavour.","exploit":"the sealing ritual, and whatever the campaign has built towards.","type":"Elemental","kind":"tier","family":"elemental","tier":"Primordial","tierNumber":5,"order":199},{"id":"old-tusker","name":"Old Tusker","kr":6,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Beast, legend","tags":["legend"],"description":"A boar the size of a cart, with one tusk broken and the other grown into a curling spear. Its hide is full of old arrowheads.","hp":60,"hpNote":null,"defence":2,"minHit":2,"speed":"40 ft","stats":{"str":6,"dex":10,"con":5,"int":16,"wis":10,"cha":15},"combat":{"melee":8,"ranged":null,"dodge":16,"disengage":14,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Tusk","text":"Tusk: 2d10.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["2d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Charge","text":"*Charge*: move at least 20 ft in a straight line, then Tusk for 3d10, +2d2 prone.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[{"dice":"2d2","n":2,"status":"prone"}]}],"traits":[{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 2."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Unkillable Legend","text":"*Unkillable Legend*: Relentless triggers twice, so it gets one more attack each of the first two times it drops to 0 HP."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"To stay king of its wood.","tactics":"Charge, vanish, charge again.","tell":"it paws the ground.","exploit":"a braced spear or a pit trap. A creature bracing a spear against the charge deals the charge damage back to it.","kind":"named","type":"Beast","builtFrom":"Wild Boar","templates":["Alpha","Boss"],"bestAs":"A starting party's first legend","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"it crashes into the trees and vanishes, then charges in next round from a random direction."},{"at":"33%","text":"it becomes fixated on whoever has hurt it most and charges them every turn."}],"lair":"In its thicket, each round one creature is caught by a falling branch or a thorn tangle (STR save or restrained).","hook":"It has killed three hunters who went after the bounty. The local lord wants its head, but the local druids want it left alone.","loot":"*Old Tusker's Spear-tusk*: a spear, 1d12, +1d10 on a charge.","order":200,"builtFromId":"wild-boar"},{"id":"greymaw-the-pack-mother","name":"Greymaw, the Pack-Mother","kr":10,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Beast, legend","tags":["legend"],"description":"A grizzled dire wolf with a white scar across her muzzle. Her pack has grown too big for its hunting grounds.","hp":84,"hpNote":null,"defence":1,"minHit":0,"speed":"50 ft","stats":{"str":7,"dex":7,"con":7,"int":15,"wis":8,"cha":14},"combat":{"melee":8,"ranged":null,"dodge":12,"disengage":8,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Bite","text":"Bite: 2d8, +2d2 prone.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["2d8"],"status":[{"dice":"2d2","n":2,"status":"prone"}]}],"traits":[{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 2."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Pack Hunter","text":"*Pack Hunter*."},{"name":"Keen Nose","text":"*Keen Nose*."},{"name":"Alpha Howl","text":"*Alpha Howl*."},{"name":"Her Pack","text":"*Her Pack*: 2d4 Wolves fight beside her as minions. They're included in her KR."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"Her cubs fed and safe.","tactics":"Lets the pack wear the party down, then takes the weakest.","tell":"the Alpha Howl.","exploit":"her cubs. Threaten them and she'll come out into the open; spare them and she may back down.","kind":"named","type":"Beast","builtFrom":"Dire Wolf","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A hunt with a moral twist","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"she howls, and 1d4 more minion Wolves arrive."},{"at":"33%","text":"the pack scatters, and she fights alone and cornered, with advantage on every attack."}],"lair":"In her den, each round a hidden wolf bursts from cover and bites one creature (1d8).","hook":"Livestock are vanishing and there's a bounty on her head. Then the party finds the den full of cubs.","loot":"*Greymaw's Pelt*: a cloak that grants advantage on tracking by scent. Wolves won't attack the wearer unless provoked.","order":201,"builtFromId":"dire-wolf"},{"id":"skitter-jack-king-of-the-sewers","name":"Skitter-Jack, King of the Sewers","kr":12,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Monstrous, cursed","tags":["cursed"],"description":"A wererat crime lord with a crown of rat skulls. Every thief in the city pays him rent.","hp":100,"hpNote":null,"defence":1,"minHit":0,"speed":"30 ft, climb 30 ft","stats":{"str":10,"dex":6,"con":8,"int":11,"wis":10,"cha":13},"combat":{"melee":8,"ranged":8,"dodge":12,"disengage":9,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Bite","text":"Bite: 1d10, plus the lycanthrope curse.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["1d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Short blade","text":"Short blade: 1d8.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["1d8"],"status":[]},{"name":"Hand crossbow","text":"Hand crossbow: range 30 ft, 1d6.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["1d6"],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 2."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Silver and Light","text":"*Silver and Light*."},{"name":"Regeneration","text":"*Regeneration*: 5 HP a turn."},{"name":"Rat Lord","text":"*Rat Lord*."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"The city's underbelly, and respect from the guilds above.","tactics":"Talks big, sends the rats, and stabs from the dark.","tell":"the rats suddenly flee towards him.","exploit":"silver. He's a coward at heart, and threatening his stash makes him negotiate.","kind":"named","type":"Monstrous","builtFrom":"Wererat","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A city underworld villain","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"he vanishes into the sewer, and 2 Rat Swarms pour out."},{"at":"33%","text":"he fully becomes a giant rat. His Bite becomes 2d8 plus the curse, and he has advantage in darkness."}],"lair":"In the sewers, each round either a sluice gate opens (STR save or be swept 20 ft) or every light goes out.","hook":"Someone stopped paying him tribute, and now the city's granaries are crawling with rats.","loot":"*The Rat Crown*: the wearer can speak with rats and command them.","order":202,"builtFromId":"wererat"},{"id":"bramm-the-toll-keeper","name":"Bramm the Toll-Keeper","kr":30,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Monstrous, giant-kin","tags":["giant-kin"],"description":"A two-headed troll that has kept the same bridge for two hundred years. The heads never stop arguing.","hp":240,"hpNote":null,"defence":3,"minHit":5,"speed":"30 ft","stats":{"str":2,"dex":11,"con":2,"int":15,"wis":11,"cha":16},"combat":{"melee":5,"ranged":null,"dodge":15,"disengage":14,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Multiattack","text":"Multiattack: Claws ×2, 3d8 each, and Bite ×2 (one per head), 2d8 each, +1d2 bleed.","multiattack":true,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["3d8","2d8"],"status":[{"dice":"1d2","n":1,"status":"bleed"}]}],"traits":[{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 1."},{"name":"Regeneration","text":"*Regeneration*: 15 HP a turn. It only stops if it took acid damage, or fire damage twice, since its last turn."},{"name":"The Toll","text":"*The Toll*: anyone who pays a fair toll (one honest secret, or a silver per head) crosses unharmed. It keeps its word absolutely, and anyone who cheats becomes its quarry."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Solo","wants":"The toll, and some decent conversation.","tactics":"Asks for the toll first. If it's refused or cheated, it fights until the cheat is in the river.","tell":"both heads stop arguing and agree on something.","exploit":"win one head over (CHA check) and the other hesitates for a turn. Or just pay.","kind":"named","type":"Monstrous","builtFrom":"Troll","templates":["Alpha"],"bestAs":"A bridge, a deal and a fight if you cheat","phases":[],"lair":"On its bridge, each round a plank gives way under one creature (Dodge roll or fall 20 ft into the river).","hook":"Everyone knows the price, but lately the toll has changed, and Bramm won't say who changed it.","loot":"*The Toll Ledger*: a record of every traveller who has crossed in two hundred years, and what they paid.","order":203,"builtFromId":"troll"},{"id":"granny-nettlebone","name":"Granny Nettlebone","kr":36,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Fey","tags":[],"description":"A hag who runs a tea-house in a cottage that's bigger inside than out. She trades curses for secrets, and the other way round.","hp":300,"hpNote":null,"defence":3,"minHit":3,"speed":"30 ft","stats":{"str":6,"dex":10,"con":6,"int":4,"wis":4,"cha":6},"combat":{"melee":6,"ranged":null,"dodge":14,"disengage":12,"casting":3},"attacks":[{"name":"Claws","text":"Claws: 2d10.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["2d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Hex","text":"*Hex*: one target makes a WIS save or has disadvantage on one stat of her choice until the hex is lifted.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Fey","text":"*Fey*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 2."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–5 of the mind and death schools."},{"name":"Illusory Appearance","text":"*Illusory Appearance*."},{"name":"Never Refuses a Fair Trade","text":"*Never Refuses a Fair Trade*: it's the one rule she can't break."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"A name, a memory or a firstborn. Anything with weight.","tactics":"Talks, bargains and only fights if a deal is broken.","tell":"she pours a cup of tea before casting a big spell.","exploit":"offer her a genuinely fair trade.","kind":"named","type":"Fey","builtFrom":"Hag","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A bargainer the party keeps coming back to","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"she splits into three. Two of them are illusions with 1 HP each."},{"at":"33%","text":"she drops her disguise. In her true form her Claws deal 3d10 and she can't use illusions."}],"lair":"In her cottage, each round the furniture attacks someone (Hurl Object, as Poltergeist), or a door leads somewhere else entirely.","hook":"Everyone in the region owes her something. One of those debts has just come due, and it's owed by someone the party cares about.","loot":"*Nettlebone's Teapot*: once a week, it answers one question truthfully, then asks the asker for a small favour.","order":204,"builtFromId":"hag"},{"id":"the-weeping-bride","name":"The Weeping Bride","kr":40,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Undead, incorporeal","tags":["incorporeal"],"description":"A bride murdered on her wedding night, still in her veil. She waits in the chapel for her groom.","hp":180,"hpNote":null,"defence":6,"minHit":0,"speed":"fly 50 ft (hover)","stats":{"str":null,"dex":4,"con":null,"int":9,"wis":5,"cha":4},"combat":{"melee":6,"ranged":null,"dodge":13,"disengage":10,"casting":4},"attacks":[{"name":"As Banshee","text":"As Banshee: Corrupting Touch, Wail and Mournful Song.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Undead","text":"*Undead*."},{"name":"Incorporeal","text":"*Incorporeal*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 2."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Sense Life","text":"*Sense Life*."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"Her murderer named.","tactics":"Pins the party with her song, then Wails.","tell":"the bells stop just before the Wail.","exploit":"anyone who's deafened is immune to the Wail. Solve her murder and she passes on peacefully.","kind":"named","type":"Undead","builtFrom":"Banshee","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A haunting with a mystery","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"her groom rises from his grave as a Wight."},{"at":"33%","text":"her Wail recharges, and she sings Mournful Song every turn."}],"lair":"In the chapel, each round the mirrors show one creature its own death (WIS save or frightened), or the wedding bells ring and drown out all speech.","hook":"The groom's family has paid priests for years to keep the chapel sealed. They know something.","loot":"*The Veil of Last Vows*: once a day, the wearer rerolls a failed save against fear.","order":205,"builtFromId":"banshee"},{"id":"varr-ironpenny-the-coin-warlord","name":"Varr Ironpenny, the Coin Warlord","kr":50,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Humanoid, general","tags":["general"],"description":"A mercenary general who will fight for anyone and betray anyone, as long as the money is right.","hp":440,"hpNote":null,"defence":5,"minHit":6,"speed":"30 ft","stats":{"str":4,"dex":9,"con":5,"int":6,"wis":6,"cha":3},"combat":{"melee":5,"ranged":null,"dodge":13,"disengage":12,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Multiattack","text":"Multiattack: Greatsword ×2, 2d10 each.","multiattack":true,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["2d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Shield slam","text":"Shield slam: 2d6, +1d2 stun.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["2d6"],"status":[{"dice":"1d2","n":1,"status":"stun"}]}],"traits":[{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 2."},{"name":"Warlord's Tempo","text":"*Warlord's Tempo* and *Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Battle Orders","text":"*Battle Orders*."},{"name":"Rally","text":"*Rally*."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"To get paid.","tactics":"Fights from the centre of his line and always keeps a way out.","tell":"he jingles his coin purse before Rally.","exploit":"outbid his employer. Steal his pay chest and his mercenaries desert.","kind":"named","type":"Humanoid","builtFrom":"Warlord","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A mercenary army's general","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"his reserve arrives, 1d4 Berserkers."},{"at":"33%","text":"he offers the party double whatever they're being paid to walk away. If they refuse, he fights with advantage on every attack."}],"lair":"In his war camp, each round a catapult shot lands on one area (Dodge roll or 3d10).","hook":"He's been hired by both sides of the same war.","loot":"*Ironpenny's Ledger*, which lists every employer he's ever had, and his war chest (2 platinum).","order":206,"builtFromId":"warlord"},{"id":"lumen-vigil-the-unbending","name":"Lumen Vigil, the Unbending","kr":56,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Celestial","tags":[],"description":"A warden angel that has guarded the same sealed door for a thousand years. It will not move.","hp":480,"hpNote":null,"defence":4,"minHit":5,"speed":"30 ft, fly 90 ft","stats":{"str":3,"dex":6,"con":4,"int":7,"wis":3,"cha":4},"combat":{"melee":5,"ranged":null,"dodge":12,"disengage":10,"casting":3},"attacks":[{"name":"As Warden Angel","text":"As Warden Angel: Light Sword ×2 and Healing Touch.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Celestial","text":"*Celestial*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–5 of the light school."},{"name":"Truesight","text":"*Truesight*."},{"name":"Shield of Wings","text":"*Shield of Wings*."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"The door kept shut, whatever it costs.","tactics":"Warns three times, then fights only as far as it needs to protect the door.","tell":"it raises its sword in salute before attacking.","exploit":"proof. If the party can show that what's behind the door has changed, or that it's needed now, it steps aside.","kind":"named","type":"Celestial","builtFrom":"Warden Angel","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A good guardian blocking the party's path","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"two Sunhounds answer its call."},{"at":"33%","text":"its wings ignite, and it can use Judgement (as High Angel) once."}],"lair":"In front of its door, each round sacred light flares, dazzling one creature (WIS save).","hook":"What the party needs is behind the door. So is whatever the angel was set to guard.","loot":"None. Befriended, it gives a blessing: once, a creature it names is healed to full when it would die.","order":207,"builtFromId":"warden-angel"},{"id":"sister-ashveil-the-plague-saint","name":"Sister Ashveil, the Plague Saint","kr":60,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Undead","tags":[],"description":"A healer who died in the plague she tried to stop. She came back believing the plague itself is a mercy.","hp":520,"hpNote":null,"defence":3,"minHit":5,"speed":"30 ft","stats":{"str":6,"dex":12,"con":null,"int":6,"wis":5,"cha":7},"combat":{"melee":5,"ranged":null,"dodge":12,"disengage":10,"casting":4},"attacks":[{"name":"As Plague Lord","text":"As Plague Lord: Censer flail and Plague Breath.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Undead","text":"*Undead*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–5 of the death school."},{"name":"Pestilent Aura","text":"*Pestilent Aura*."},{"name":"Rot Host","text":"*Rot Host*. 2d6 Plague Corpses shuffle around her as minions."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"To \"cleanse\" the world, as she sees it, with mercy.","tactics":"Preaches while her corpses advance, and breathes on anyone who bunches up.","tell":"she blesses the air before Plague Breath.","exploit":"she truly believes she's helping. Showing her a cure (or someone she failed to save) makes her hesitate for a turn.","kind":"named","type":"Undead","builtFrom":"Plague Lord","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A villain who thinks she's merciful","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"her censer cracks, and a permanent plague cloud fills everything within 30 ft of her (strength save each turn or poisoned)."},{"at":"33%","text":"she drinks what's left in the censer and becomes incorporeal."}],"lair":"In her chapel, each round the bells toll (WIS save or frightened), or one Plague Corpse bursts.","hook":"Her followers are spreading through the villages, offering a \"cure\".","loot":"*Censer of the Last Mercy*: once a day, it either cures one disease or spreads one.","order":208,"builtFromId":"plague-lord"},{"id":"rustmaw-the-furnace-bull","name":"Rustmaw, the Furnace Bull","kr":60,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Construct","tags":[],"description":"A huge bronze bull, green with age, built to guard a vault for a bloodline that has since died out, or so everyone thinks.","hp":540,"hpNote":null,"defence":5,"minHit":7,"speed":"40 ft","stats":{"str":1,"dex":13,"con":null,"int":19,"wis":12,"cha":19},"combat":{"melee":5,"ranged":null,"dodge":15,"disengage":14,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Horns","text":"Horns: 4d10.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["4d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Charge","text":"*Charge*: move at least 20 ft in a straight line, then Horns for 5d10, +3d2 prone.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[{"dice":"3d2","n":3,"status":"prone"}]},{"name":"Furnace Breath","text":"*Furnace Breath* (3-turn recharge): a 30 ft cone, 7d10, +3d2 burn. A Dodge roll halves the damage.","multiattack":false,"recharge":3,"limit":null,"damage":["7d10"],"status":[{"dice":"3d2","n":3,"status":"burn"}]}],"traits":[{"name":"Construct","text":"*Construct*."},{"name":"Mindless","text":"*Mindless*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*. Immune to fire."},{"name":"Overpressure","text":"*Overpressure*: steam vents from its joints whenever it's hit by a crit, dealing 2d6 to everyone next to it."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"To guard the vault until its makers' bloodline returns.","tactics":"Charges, breathes, and charges again.","tell":"its furnace glows white through its ribs.","exploit":"cold water in the furnace shuts down its breath for 1d4 turns. A descendant of its makers can command it to stop.","kind":"named","type":"Construct","builtFrom":"Bronze Bull","templates":["Alpha","Boss"],"bestAs":"A vault guardian","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"its furnace overloads, and anyone who starts their turn within 10 ft takes 2d6 burn."},{"at":"33%","text":"it breaks loose of its programming and charges every turn, and its breath recharges in 2 turns."}],"lair":"In the vault, each round jets of fire burst from floor vents along one line (Dodge roll or 4d10).","hook":"The bloodline isn't extinct. One of the party might be part of it.","loot":"*Rustmaw's Furnace Core*: an everlasting forge-fire. A smith's dream.","order":209,"builtFromId":"bronze-bull"},{"id":"the-briar-prince","name":"The Briar Prince","kr":68,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Fey","tags":[],"description":"A prince of a fey court, beautiful and bored. He collects duels the way others collect art.","hp":560,"hpNote":null,"defence":5,"minHit":6,"speed":"40 ft (60 ft mounted)","stats":{"str":4,"dex":4,"con":5,"int":7,"wis":6,"cha":3},"combat":{"melee":5,"ranged":null,"dodge":10,"disengage":8,"casting":5},"attacks":[{"name":"As Fey Knight","text":"As Fey Knight: Glass Blade ×2 and Court Glamour.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Fey","text":"*Fey*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Step Through","text":"*Step Through*."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"A worthy duel, or a mortal to bring back to court.","tactics":"Challenges the best fighter to a duel, and only fights the whole party if they cheat.","tell":"he bows.","exploit":"cold iron. A formal duel binds him to whatever terms are agreed.","kind":"named","type":"Fey","builtFrom":"Fey Knight","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A court intrigue that ends in a duel","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"his court arrives: two Sprites and a Redcap."},{"at":"33%","text":"he drops the courtesies. His blades deal an extra 1d10, and Step Through becomes free every turn."}],"lair":"In his hedge maze, each round one wall moves up to 20 ft, splitting the party or trapping someone.","hook":"A villager has vanished from their wedding. She's now his \"guest\".","loot":"*Thornglass Rapier*: 1d12, +1d2 bleed, and the wielder can Step Through once a day.","order":210,"builtFromId":"fey-knight"},{"id":"kragmaul-king-of-the-hill","name":"Kragmaul, King of the Hill","kr":84,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Monstrous, giant","tags":["giant"],"description":"Thirty feet tall, wearing a boulder as a crown. He rules a court of ogres from a hill fort built out of other people's houses.","hp":660,"hpNote":null,"defence":3,"minHit":8,"speed":"40 ft","stats":{"str":1,"dex":14,"con":2,"int":15,"wis":13,"cha":14},"combat":{"melee":4,"ranged":6,"dodge":16,"disengage":16,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Tree-trunk club","text":"Tree-trunk club: reach 15 ft, 4d20.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["4d20"],"status":[]},{"name":"Boulder","text":"Boulder: range 120 ft, 4d12, +2d2 prone.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["4d12"],"status":[{"dice":"2d2","n":2,"status":"prone"}]},{"name":"Stomp","text":"*Stomp*: everyone within 20 ft takes 3d12, +3d2 prone.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["3d12"],"status":[{"dice":"3d2","n":3,"status":"prone"}]}],"traits":[{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Dim","text":"*Dim*."},{"name":"Huge","text":"*Huge*."},{"name":"Earthshaker","text":"*Earthshaker* (Alpha)."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"Tribute, mostly food.","tactics":"Throws boulders at anyone approaching his fort, then stomps whoever gets close.","tell":"he lifts one foot high before a Stomp.","exploit":"he's very easy to flatter. Challenge him to an eating contest and he can't say no.","kind":"named","type":"Monstrous","builtFrom":"Hill Giant","templates":["Alpha","Boss"],"bestAs":"A giant warlord","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"he hurls his throne at the party (5d12 in a 20 ft area)."},{"at":"33%","text":"his ogre court charges in: 2 Ogres."}],"lair":"In his hill fort, each round a rockslide crashes down one slope (Dodge roll or 3d10 and prone).","hook":"Three villages are already paying him tribute. The fourth refused.","loot":"*Kragmaul's Crown*: a ring of iron the size of a shield. It works as a shield that also grants advantage on saves against being knocked prone.","order":211,"builtFromId":"hill-giant"},{"id":"mother-brine-the-ship-eater","name":"Mother Brine, the Ship-Eater","kr":120,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Monstrous, aquatic","tags":["aquatic"],"description":"An abyssal squid older than any sailor's tale. She lives in a graveyard of wrecks, and some of the ships are still crewed by her victims.","hp":1125,"hpNote":null,"defence":5,"minHit":10,"speed":"swim 80 ft","stats":{"str":1,"dex":6,"con":1,"int":9,"wis":5,"cha":15},"combat":{"melee":3,"ranged":null,"dodge":13,"disengage":11,"casting":null},"attacks":[{"name":"Multiattack","text":"Multiattack: Tentacles ×4, reach 40 ft, 3d10 each, and the target is grabbed.","multiattack":true,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["3d10"],"status":[]},{"name":"Beak on a grabbed target","text":"Beak on a grabbed target: 6d12.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["6d12"],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Squid's Tempo","text":"*Squid's Tempo*."},{"name":"Ink Night","text":"*Ink Night*."},{"name":"Whirlpool","text":"*Whirlpool*: 600 ft."},{"name":"Graveyard of Wrecks","text":"*Graveyard of Wrecks* (Alpha): each round, 1d4 Drowned Sailors climb out of her wrecks and attack the nearest ship."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Solo","wants":"Every ship that crosses her waters.","tactics":"Drags ships in, grabs the crew and feeds them to her beak.","tell":"the sea goes glassy and still, then the whirlpool starts.","exploit":"severed tentacles stay severed. Brought onto land, she's helpless.","kind":"named","type":"Monstrous","builtFrom":"Abyssal Squid","templates":["Alpha"],"bestAs":"A sea legend","phases":[],"lair":"In her graveyard, each round one wreck shifts and rams a ship (4d12 hull damage), or the whirlpool pulls twice as hard.","hook":"The fastest trade route now runs straight through her waters, and someone is paying captains to take it anyway.","loot":"*Brine's Pearl*: the holder can breathe underwater, and once a day can turn a current or a tide.","order":212,"builtFromId":"abyssal-squid"},{"id":"the-thousand-eyed-choir","name":"The Thousand-Eyed Choir","kr":120,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Aberration","tags":[],"description":"A Many-Mouthed that has been absorbing a city's lost and forgotten for a century. Every voice it has eaten still sings inside it.","hp":1100,"hpNote":null,"defence":3,"minHit":8,"speed":"20 ft, climb 20 ft","stats":{"str":2,"dex":16,"con":1,"int":6,"wis":3,"cha":16},"combat":{"melee":5,"ranged":null,"dodge":17,"disengage":17,"casting":4},"attacks":[{"name":"As The Many-Mouthed","text":"As The Many-Mouthed: Bites against everyone within 10 ft.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Aberration","text":"*Aberration*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Boss Tempo","text":"*Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Gibbering","text":"*Gibbering*."},{"name":"Absorb","text":"*Absorb*."},{"name":"Voices of the Lost","text":"*Voices of the Lost*: it can speak in the voice of anyone it has absorbed."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"Every voice in the city in its choir.","tactics":"Lures people down with the voices of their lost loved ones, then swallows them.","tell":"the voices fall into a single chord.","exploit":"deafened creatures are immune to Gibbering. Fire and ranged attacks keep it from reaching a group.","kind":"named","type":"Aberration","builtFrom":"The Many-Mouthed","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"Cosmic horror under the city","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"each turn it splits off 1d4 Spawnlings."},{"at":"33%","text":"the choir sings as one, and saves against Gibbering are made at disadvantage."}],"lair":"In its flesh cavern, each round the walls grab one creature (STR save or restrained).","hook":"Missing-persons notices pile up, and people swear they've heard the missing calling from the drains.","loot":"*The Choir Stone*, a crystal left in its core. Whoever holds it can speak and understand any language.","order":213,"builtFromId":"the-many-mouthed"},{"id":"the-grey-abbot","name":"The Grey Abbot","kr":170,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Undead","tags":[],"description":"A lich who was once the head of a great library-monastery. His monks still serve him, centuries after their deaths.","hp":1300,"hpNote":null,"defence":6,"minHit":8,"speed":"30 ft","stats":{"str":12,"dex":8,"con":null,"int":1,"wis":2,"cha":3},"combat":{"melee":9,"ranged":null,"dodge":13,"disengage":10,"casting":1},"attacks":[{"name":"As Lich","text":"As Lich: Paralysing Touch, Death Bolt and Raise Horde.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":[],"status":[]}],"traits":[{"name":"Undead","text":"*Undead*."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Lich's Tempo","text":"*Lich's Tempo* and *Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–9 in the death and mind schools."},{"name":"Magic Resistant","text":"*Magic Resistant*."},{"name":"Soul Vessel","text":"*Soul Vessel*: his soul vessel is one book hidden among ten thousand."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"The last missing page of a forbidden book.","tactics":"Fights behind a wall of dead monks, and saves his best spells for whoever goes for his books.","tell":"the candles all lean towards him before Raise Horde.","exploit":"find the right book. He'll protect it above everything else, which gives it away.","kind":"named","type":"Undead","builtFrom":"Lich","templates":["Boss"],"bestAs":"A long-game mastermind","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"the library's dead monks rise, 2d6 Skeletons and a Wight."},{"at":"33%","text":"Raise Horde recharges every round, and his Death Bolts hit twice."}],"lair":"In the library, each round the books scream (WIS save or confused for 1 turn), or a bookshelf topples (Dodge roll or 4d10 and pinned).","hook":"The party has the missing page, or a lead to it. He's polite, patient and willing to pay. For now.","loot":"His spellbook (tier 7–9 spells), and the forbidden book itself.","order":214,"builtFromId":"lich"},{"id":"vhalrikka-the-last-ember","name":"Vhalrikka, the Last Ember","kr":240,"section":"Named monsters","typeLine":"Dragon","tags":[],"description":"The last fire dragon of her line, with a second pair of horns and a crest of crystal scales. Her egg was stolen a century ago, and she has been burning kingdoms to find it ever since.","hp":2400,"hpNote":null,"defence":6,"minHit":10,"speed":"40 ft, fly 80 ft","stats":{"str":2,"dex":6,"con":2,"int":5,"wis":5,"cha":4},"combat":{"melee":3,"ranged":3,"dodge":11,"disengage":9,"casting":4},"attacks":[{"name":"Multiattack","text":"Multiattack: Bite 3d20, +3d2 burn, and Claws ×2, 3d12 each.","multiattack":true,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["3d20","3d12"],"status":[{"dice":"3d2","n":3,"status":"burn"}]},{"name":"Tail","text":"Tail: reach 20 ft, 3d12, +2d2 prone.","multiattack":false,"recharge":null,"limit":null,"damage":["3d12"],"status":[{"dice":"2d2","n":2,"status":"prone"}]},{"name":"Breath","text":"*Breath* (2-turn recharge): two 90 ft cones, 11d10 each, +6d2 burn. A Dodge roll halves the damage.","multiattack":false,"recharge":2,"limit":null,"damage":["11d10"],"status":[{"dice":"6d2","n":6,"status":"burn"}]}],"traits":[{"name":"Dragon","text":"*Dragon*, Fire flavour (change it if you like)."},{"name":"Solo","text":"*Solo*, Defiant 3."},{"name":"Dragon's Tempo","text":"*Dragon's Tempo* and *Boss Tempo*."},{"name":"Frightful Presence","text":"*Frightful Presence*."},{"name":"Spellcasting","text":"*Spellcasting*: tiers 1–4."},{"name":"Inferno Trail","text":"*Inferno Trail* (Fire signature move)."},{"name":"Twin Breath","text":"*Twin Breath* (Alpha)."}],"harvest":null,"role":"Boss","wants":"Her egg, and whoever took it.","tactics":"Interrogates before she burns. She'll spare anyone who can point her to the egg.","tell":"her crest glows like a forge before Breath.","exploit":"the egg. Return it, or even prove where it is, and the fight ends.","kind":"named","type":"Dragon","builtFrom":"Adult Fire Dragon","templates":["Alpha","Boss"],"bestAs":"A campaign finale","phases":[{"at":"66%","text":"she takes to the sky and rains fire, so for 2 rounds the party can only reach her with ranged attacks."},{"at":"33%","text":"grief takes over. All her statuses clear, her Breath recharges, and she fights to the death unless shown the egg."}],"lair":"In her volcano, each round lava geysers burst under one creature (Dodge roll or 6d10 burn), or the cavern fills with ash and everything beyond 20 ft goes dark.","hook":"The egg is still alive, and it's in the possession of someone powerful the party knows.","loot":"Her hoard. If she's befriended, a scale from her crest (legendary core) and a dragon's favour.","order":215,"builtFromId":"adult-dragon","flavour":"Fire"}]}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('templates', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","alpha":{"name":"Alpha","rules":"Any creature in this book can be an **Alpha**, except a Primordial. An Alpha is the undiluted, oversized version that leads its kind, the way the Prime races relate to the playable races. Apply these changes to the creature's stat block:\n\n- **KR ×1.5**, rounded up. **HP ×1.5**. **Defence +1**, **Min hit +2**.\n- Every base stat and combat stat improves by 1, to a minimum of 1.\n- Every attack adds one more of its damage die, so a 2d8 bite becomes 3d8. Every status roll gets +1d2.\n- It has **one exaggerated physical divergence** and **one new signature trait**.\n- An Alpha dragon or elemental sits between two tiers. An Alpha Adult Dragon is KR 120.\n- Humanoids don't get Alphas. Use the race's Prime version instead.","maths":{"krMultiplier":1.5,"krRound":"up","hpMultiplier":1.5,"defence":1,"minHit":2,"statImprove":1,"statMinimum":1,"extraDamageDie":1,"extraStatusD2":1},"notAllowed":{"types":["Humanoid"],"tiers":["Primordial"]},"alphas":[{"name":"Alpha Wolf","kr":2,"divergence":"Twice the size, with a silver-white mane","signature":{"name":"Pack Leader","limit":null,"text":"every wolf within 60 ft has Pack Hunter even when it's alone. If the Alpha dies, the pack flees."},"signatureText":"*Pack Leader*: every wolf within 60 ft has Pack Hunter even when it's alone. If the Alpha dies, the pack flees.","baseId":"wolf"},{"name":"Rat King","kr":2,"divergence":"A knot of rats fused at the tails, moving as one","signature":{"name":"Plague Tide","limit":null,"text":"anyone who touches a creature it has infected makes the disease save too."},"signatureText":"*Plague Tide*: anyone who touches a creature it has infected makes the disease save too.","baseId":"rat-swarm"},{"name":"Ossuary Champion","kr":2,"divergence":"An eight-foot skeleton with a second pair of arms","signature":{"name":"Four Arms","limit":null,"text":"it makes two extra weapon attacks."},"signatureText":"*Four Arms*: it makes two extra weapon attacks.","baseId":"skeleton"},{"name":"Abomination","kr":2,"divergence":"Several corpses stitched into one hulk","signature":{"name":"Many Mouths","limit":null,"text":"it Bites every creature it's grabbing."},"signatureText":"*Many Mouths*: it Bites every creature it's grabbing.","baseId":"zombie"},{"name":"Alpha Bear","kr":5,"divergence":"Shoulders like a hill, with bone plates under the fur","signature":{"name":"Unstoppable","limit":null,"text":"it can't be knocked prone, grabbed or pushed."},"signatureText":"*Unstoppable*: it can't be knocked prone, grabbed or pushed.","baseId":"brown-bear"},{"name":"Brood Mother","kr":6,"divergence":"A bloated body crawling with young","signature":{"name":"Brood","limit":"once per combat","text":"it releases a swarm of spiderlings. Use Rat Swarm stats with poison instead of disease."},"signatureText":"*Brood* (once per combat): it releases a swarm of spiderlings. Use Rat Swarm stats with poison instead of disease.","baseId":"giant-spider"},{"name":"Ghast","kr":6,"divergence":"Jaw unhinged, with a battlefield stench","signature":{"name":"Stench","limit":null,"text":"creatures that start their turn within 10 ft make a strength save or are poisoned."},"signatureText":"*Stench*: creatures that start their turn within 10 ft make a strength save or are poisoned.","baseId":"ghoul"},{"name":"Ogre Warlord","kr":12,"divergence":"Tusked, scarred and plated in looted armour","signature":{"name":"Bully","limit":null,"text":"allies within 30 ft have advantage on attacks against prone targets."},"signatureText":"*Bully*: allies within 30 ft have advantage on attacks against prone targets.","baseId":"ogre"},{"name":"Alpha Troll","kr":30,"divergence":"Two heads and stone-grey hide","signature":{"name":"Twin Heads","limit":null,"text":"two Bites, and it only stops regenerating if it took fire or acid damage twice since its last turn."},"signatureText":"*Twin Heads*: two Bites, and it only stops regenerating if it took fire or acid damage twice since its last turn.","baseId":"troll"},{"name":"Hill Giant Chief","kr":42,"divergence":"Thirty feet tall, wearing a boulder as a crown","signature":{"name":"Earthshaker","limit":null,"text":"its Stomp hits everyone within 20 ft."},"signatureText":"*Earthshaker*: its Stomp hits everyone within 20 ft.","baseId":"hill-giant"},{"name":"Worm Matriarch","kr":60,"divergence":"Three hundred feet long, with a cavern for a mouth","signature":{"name":"Undertow","limit":null,"text":"each round, the sand within 100 ft drags everyone 10 ft towards it."},"signatureText":"*Undertow*: each round, the sand within 100 ft drags everyone 10 ft towards it.","baseId":"sandworm"},{"name":"Alpha Adult Dragon","kr":120,"divergence":"A second pair of horns and a crest of crystal scales","signature":{"name":"Twin Breath","limit":null,"text":"its breath recharges in 2 turns and can split into two cones."},"signatureText":"*Twin Breath*: its breath recharges in 2 turns and can split into two cones.","baseId":"adult-dragon"}]},"group":{"name":"Group","rules":"A group of creatures gets more actions than their KRs add up to. After adding up the KRs of creatures that act separately, multiply the total:\n\n- 3–6 creatures: ×1.25\n- 7–12 creatures: ×1.5\n- 13 or more: ×2\n\nMinions don't count towards group size. Examples: four wolves are KR 4 × 1.25 = 5. A Bandit Captain with four Bandits is KR 9 × 1.25 = 11.","bands":[{"min":3,"max":6,"multiplier":1.25},{"min":7,"max":12,"multiplier":1.5},{"min":13,"max":null,"multiplier":2}],"minionsCount":false},"minion":{"name":"Minion","rules":"Any creature of KR 8 or lower can be run as a minion, for hordes, armies or a necromancer's dead.\n\n- **KR ÷5**, so five minion wolves are KR 1.\n- **1 HP.** Any hit that deals damage kills it, but it still gets its Dodge roll.\n- Its attacks deal their average damage with no roll, and at most +1d2 status. It has no recharge abilities and no Tempo.","maxKr":8,"krDivisor":5,"hp":1,"maxStatusD2":1,"averageDamage":true,"noRecharge":true,"noTempo":true},"boss":{"name":"Boss","rules":"Use this for a creature that carries a whole fight on its own.\n\n- **KR ×2, HP ×2.** It counts as Solo, with Defiant 2, or Defiant 3 at KR 50+.\n- **Boss Tempo**: one extra action at the end of each round, on top of any Tempo it already has.\n- **Phases**: at 66% and 33% HP it clears all its statuses and recharges one ability. Then pick one: the arena changes (collapse, flood, fire or darkness); it gains a new attack; it calls allies worth up to 10% of its KR; or it changes tactics completely (takes to the air, falls back to a second room, or turns on its own minions).\n- **Lair actions**: in its lair, at the top of each round, it uses one lair effect. Use its flavour's lair effect, or one from its Tactics line.\n- It stacks with the Alpha template. Apply Alpha first, then Boss.","krMultiplier":2,"hpMultiplier":2,"defiant":2,"defiantAt50":3,"defiantKrThreshold":50,"bossTempo":1,"phaseAt":["66%","33%"],"stacksWithAlpha":"Apply Alpha first, then Boss."}}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('statuses', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","rules":"Each 2 on the status dice applies one stack. *Hard control* means stun, paralysis, sleep, frozen solid and petrification. When a hard control ends, the creature can't be hard-controlled again until the end of its next turn.","hardControl":["Stun","Paralysis","Sleep","Freeze (frozen solid)","Petrification"],"statuses":[{"id":"burn","name":"Burn","names":["Burn"],"perStack":"1d6 fire at the start of its turn","max":"None","ends":"Loses 1 stack a turn. Water, or an action to smother it, clears all"},{"id":"bleed","name":"Bleed","names":["Bleed"],"perStack":"1d4 at the start of its turn","max":"None","ends":"Loses 1 stack a turn. Any healing clears all"},{"id":"poison","name":"Poison","names":["Poison"],"perStack":"1 damage at the start of its turn, and −1 to all rolls","max":"−5 to rolls","ends":"A STR save at the end of each turn removes 1 stack. Clears after combat"},{"id":"disease","name":"Disease","names":["Disease"],"perStack":"One step towards sickness. At 3 stacks it catches the disease","max":"3","ends":"Loses 1 stack per long rest, or with medicine"},{"id":"madness","name":"Madness","names":["Madness"],"perStack":"At the start of its turn, roll a d20. If the roll is equal to or under its stacks, it acts randomly","max":"10","ends":"Loses 1 stack per long rest, or with a tier 3 cleansing"},{"id":"wither","name":"Wither","names":["Wither"],"perStack":"−1d10 max HP","max":"None","ends":"Long rest"},{"id":"corrode","name":"Corrode","names":["Corrode"],"perStack":"−1 armour Min hit","max":"None","ends":"Repair"},{"id":"freeze","name":"Freeze","names":["Freeze"],"perStack":"−10 ft speed. At 3 stacks it's frozen solid (hard control) for 1 turn, then clears","max":"3","ends":"Fire clears all"},{"id":"stun","name":"Stun, paralysis","names":["Stun","Paralysis"],"perStack":"1 turn","max":"2 turns","ends":"Hard control"},{"id":"sleep","name":"Sleep","names":["Sleep"],"perStack":"Asleep 1 turn","max":"2 turns","ends":"Hard control. Damage wakes it"},{"id":"blinded","name":"Blinded, dazzled, deafened, disorientated","names":["Blinded","Dazzled","Deafened","Disorientated"],"perStack":"1 turn. Dazzled means disadvantage on attacks","max":"3 turns","ends":"Ends when the duration runs out"},{"id":"charmed","name":"Charmed, frightened, confused","names":["Charmed","Frightened","Confused"],"perStack":"1 turn","max":"3 turns","ends":"A WIS save at the end of each turn ends it"},{"id":"prone","name":"Prone, stagger","names":["Prone","Stagger"],"perStack":"Knocked down, or loses its reaction","max":"1","ends":"Standing up costs half its movement"},{"id":"knockback","name":"Knockback","names":["Knockback"],"perStack":"10 ft","max":"None","ends":"Instant"},{"id":"restrained","name":"Restrained, grabbed, entangled, crushed","names":["Restrained","Grabbed","Entangled","Crushed"],"perStack":"No stacks","max":"1","ends":"A STR save to escape"}]}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('kr-budget', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","rules":"This is the budget every stat block is tuned to. It's based on your players' numbers. Level 0 adventurers have about 15–35 HP, stats around 11 and hit for 1d6–1d8. Level 11 adventurers have 28–55 HP plus up to 75 armour temp HP, Melee 5–14 and Dodge 10–16, and hit for 1d20 to 1d50+10.\n- **Dodge by role**: Brute +3, Huge another +2 (to a maximum of 20), Skirmisher −2, Lurker −1, and Tiny or evasive fliers −4 (never below 8).\n- **Damage per round** counts every action it gets in a round, including Tempo. Melee and Ranged never go below 3. Set pieces ignore the budget.","rows":[{"kr":"½–1","krMin":0.5,"krMax":1,"hp":"5–14","hpMin":5,"hpMax":14,"meleeRanged":"9","meleeRangedBest":9,"meleeRangedWorst":9,"dodge":14,"damagePerRound":"3–5","dprMin":3,"dprMax":5,"minHit":"0","minHitMin":0,"minHitMax":0},{"kr":"2–3","krMin":2,"krMax":3,"hp":"14–35","hpMin":14,"hpMax":35,"meleeRanged":"9–8","meleeRangedBest":8,"meleeRangedWorst":9,"dodge":14,"damagePerRound":"6–9","dprMin":6,"dprMax":9,"minHit":"0–2","minHitMin":0,"minHitMax":2},{"kr":"4–6","krMin":4,"krMax":6,"hp":"30–60","hpMin":30,"hpMax":60,"meleeRanged":"8","meleeRangedBest":8,"meleeRangedWorst":8,"dodge":14,"damagePerRound":"9–13","dprMin":9,"dprMax":13,"minHit":"0–3","minHitMin":0,"minHitMax":3},{"kr":"8–14","krMin":8,"krMax":14,"hp":"60–130","hpMin":60,"hpMax":130,"meleeRanged":"7","meleeRangedBest":7,"meleeRangedWorst":7,"dodge":13,"damagePerRound":"14–21","dprMin":14,"dprMax":21,"minHit":"2–4","minHitMin":2,"minHitMax":4},{"kr":"15–24","krMin":15,"krMax":24,"hp":"100–200","hpMin":100,"hpMax":200,"meleeRanged":"6","meleeRangedBest":6,"meleeRangedWorst":6,"dodge":13,"damagePerRound":"22–30","dprMin":22,"dprMax":30,"minHit":"3–5","minHitMin":3,"minHitMax":5},{"kr":"25–45","krMin":25,"krMax":45,"hp":"200–380","hpMin":200,"hpMax":380,"meleeRanged":"5","meleeRangedBest":5,"meleeRangedWorst":5,"dodge":12,"damagePerRound":"30–45","dprMin":30,"dprMax":45,"minHit":"4–7","minHitMin":4,"minHitMax":7},{"kr":"50–90","krMin":50,"krMax":90,"hp":"380–800","hpMin":380,"hpMax":800,"meleeRanged":"4","meleeRangedBest":4,"meleeRangedWorst":4,"dodge":12,"damagePerRound":"45–80","dprMin":45,"dprMax":80,"minHit":"6–9","minHitMin":6,"minHitMax":9},{"kr":"100–200","krMin":100,"krMax":200,"hp":"900–2,000","hpMin":900,"hpMax":2000,"meleeRanged":"3","meleeRangedBest":3,"meleeRangedWorst":3,"dodge":11,"damagePerRound":"80–145","dprMin":80,"dprMax":145,"minHit":"9–12","minHitMin":9,"minHitMax":12},{"kr":"225–600","krMin":225,"krMax":600,"hp":"2,200–6,000","hpMin":2200,"hpMax":6000,"meleeRanged":"3","meleeRangedBest":3,"meleeRangedWorst":3,"dodge":10,"damagePerRound":"150–350","dprMin":150,"dprMax":350,"minHit":"11–14","minHitMin":11,"minHitMax":14}]}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('harvest', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","rules":"Coin in a stat block is what the creature carries, on top of its harvest. Run every value through your price tool for settlement size, supply and reputation.","parts":[{"id":"common-part","part":"Common part","examples":"pelt, hide, fangs, meat, chitin, feathers","text":"Common part: pelt, hide, fangs, meat, chitin, feathers","value":"KR × 10 silver","perKr":10,"currency":"silver"},{"id":"reagent","part":"Reagent","examples":"venom, blood, gland, dust, essence, ichor, spores","text":"Reagent: venom, blood, gland, dust, essence, ichor, spores","value":"KR × 50 silver","perKr":50,"currency":"silver"},{"id":"legendary-core","part":"Legendary core","examples":"anything called a heartscale, core or heart, from KR 100+","text":"Legendary core: anything called a heartscale, core or heart, from KR 100+","value":"KR × 1 gold","perKr":1,"currency":"gold"},{"id":"god-tier-core","part":"God-tier core","examples":"from a Primordial, Archfiend, Colossus, Titan or similar","text":"God-tier core: from a Primordial, Archfiend, Colossus, Titan or similar","value":"KR × 5 gold","perKr":5,"currency":"gold"}]}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('flavours', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","rules":"Pick one flavour for any dragon or elemental. The status is what each 2 on its status dice applies. It takes double damage from the flavour in \"Weak to\", and it's immune to its own. Creation and Destruction are god-tier, so they only exist at Ancient and Primordial.","signatureRules":"Every dragon and elemental gets its flavour's signature move from Adult upwards, and the upgrade from Ancient upwards. Creation and Destruction start at Ancient, so they get the first move there and the upgrade at Primordial.","signatureFrom":{"normal":{"move":"Adult","upgrade":"Ancient"},"godTier":{"move":"Ancient","upgrade":"Primordial"}},"godTierFrom":"Ancient","flavours":[{"id":"fire","name":"Fire","path":"Element","pathKind":"Element","pathOf":[],"school":null,"status":"Burn","statusName":"burn","weakTo":"Water","movement":"50 ft","lair":"Ground smoulders: 1d10 burn to anyone ending a turn on it","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Inferno Trail","limit":null,"text":"its flight leaves a 10 ft-wide trail of fire for a round, 2d6 burn to anyone crossing it","cell":"*Inferno Trail*: its flight leaves a 10 ft-wide trail of fire for a round, 2d6 burn to anyone crossing it"},"upgrade":{"name":null,"limit":null,"text":"The trail becomes a 30 ft wall that lasts 3 rounds, 4d6 burn","cell":"The trail becomes a 30 ft wall that lasts 3 rounds, 4d6 burn"}},{"id":"water","name":"Water","path":"Element","pathKind":"Element","pathOf":[],"school":null,"status":"Knockback 10 ft","statusName":"knockback 10 ft","weakTo":"Cold","movement":"Swim 60 ft","lair":"Waist-deep water: half speed unless swimming","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Undertow","limit":null,"text":"once a round, a creature that moves within 20 ft makes a STR save or is pulled 10 ft towards it","cell":"*Undertow*: once a round, a creature that moves within 20 ft makes a STR save or is pulled 10 ft towards it"},"upgrade":{"name":"Tidal Prison","limit":null,"text":"one creature is sealed in a sphere of water (restrained, can't breathe) until it passes a STR save or deals 30 damage to it","cell":"*Tidal Prison*: one creature is sealed in a sphere of water (restrained, can't breathe) until it passes a STR save or deals 30 damage to it"}},{"id":"earth","name":"Earth","path":"Element","pathKind":"Element","pathOf":[],"school":null,"status":"Stun","statusName":"stun","weakTo":"Water","movement":"Burrow 30 ft","lair":"Tremors: STR save each round or prone","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Tremor Step","limit":null,"text":"when it lands or stomps, everyone within 20 ft makes a Dodge roll or is knocked prone","cell":"*Tremor Step*: when it lands or stomps, everyone within 20 ft makes a Dodge roll or is knocked prone"},"upgrade":{"name":"Mountain's Hide","limit":null,"text":"once per combat, its Min hit rises by 5 for 2 rounds","cell":"*Mountain's Hide*: once per combat, its Min hit rises by 5 for 2 rounds"}},{"id":"air","name":"Air","path":"Element","pathKind":"Element","pathOf":[],"school":null,"status":"Disorientate","statusName":"disorientate","weakTo":"Earth","movement":"Fly 80 ft (hover)","lair":"Gale: disadvantage on ranged attacks, and fliers make a STR save or are blown 20 ft","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Slipstream","limit":null,"text":"it can Disengage for free every turn, and ranged attacks against it have disadvantage","cell":"*Slipstream*: it can Disengage for free every turn, and ranged attacks against it have disadvantage"},"upgrade":{"name":"Cyclone","limit":null,"text":"a 30 ft whirlwind it steers lifts creatures and flings them 30 ft","cell":"*Cyclone*: a 30 ft whirlwind it steers lifts creatures and flings them 30 ft"}},{"id":"smoke","name":"Smoke","path":"Hybrid (Fire, Air)","pathKind":"Hybrid","pathOf":["Fire","Air"],"school":null,"status":"Choking (poisoned)","statusName":"choking","weakTo":"Water","movement":"Fly 50 ft","lair":"Thick haze: can't see beyond 10 ft","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Smokescreen","limit":null,"text":"as a reaction to being targeted, it becomes hidden in smoke until its next turn","cell":"*Smokescreen*: as a reaction to being targeted, it becomes hidden in smoke until its next turn"},"upgrade":{"name":"Choking Pall","limit":null,"text":"its smoke is poisonous, +2d2 poison a turn inside it","cell":"*Choking Pall*: its smoke is poisonous, +2d2 poison a turn inside it"}},{"id":"steam","name":"Steam","path":"Hybrid (Fire, Water)","pathKind":"Hybrid","pathOf":["Fire","Water"],"school":null,"status":"Scald (burn, ignores Min hit)","statusName":"scald","weakTo":"Cold","movement":"Fly 40 ft","lair":"Scalding fog: 1d6 burn a turn, can't see beyond 20 ft","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Scalding Hiss","limit":null,"text":"any creature that hits it in melee takes 1d10 burn","cell":"*Scalding Hiss*: any creature that hits it in melee takes 1d10 burn"},"upgrade":{"name":"Pressure Burst","limit":"once per combat","text":"it explodes in steam, 8d10 to everything within 60 ft, pushing it all 20 ft away","cell":"*Pressure Burst* (once per combat): it explodes in steam, 8d10 to everything within 60 ft, pushing it all 20 ft away"}},{"id":"cold","name":"Cold","path":"Hybrid (Air, Water)","pathKind":"Hybrid","pathOf":["Air","Water"],"school":null,"status":"Freeze","statusName":"freeze","weakTo":"Fire","movement":"Ice-glide 50 ft","lair":"Ice: Dodge roll or prone when you move more than half speed","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Frozen Ground","limit":null,"text":"the ground within 30 ft of it is always ice","cell":"*Frozen Ground*: the ground within 30 ft of it is always ice"},"upgrade":{"name":"Shatter","limit":null,"text":"creatures that are frozen solid take double damage from its attacks","cell":"*Shatter*: creatures that are frozen solid take double damage from its attacks"}},{"id":"sand","name":"Sand","path":"Hybrid (Air, Earth)","pathKind":"Hybrid","pathOf":["Air","Earth"],"school":null,"status":"Blinded","statusName":"blinded","weakTo":"Water","movement":"Burrow 40 ft","lair":"Sandstorm and sinking sand: STR save or restrained","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Sandswim","limit":null,"text":"it moves through sand at full speed and erupts to attack with advantage","cell":"*Sandswim*: it moves through sand at full speed and erupts to attack with advantage"},"upgrade":{"name":"Hourglass","limit":"once per combat","text":"everything within 60 ft becomes sinking sand","cell":"*Hourglass* (once per combat): everything within 60 ft becomes sinking sand"}},{"id":"mud","name":"Mud","path":"Hybrid (Water, Earth)","pathKind":"Hybrid","pathOf":["Water","Earth"],"school":null,"status":"Slowed","statusName":"slowed","weakTo":"Fire","movement":"Burrow 20 ft, swim 30 ft","lair":"Sucking mud: half speed, and no Disengage","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Clinging Mire","limit":null,"text":"creatures it hits can't Disengage until their next turn","cell":"*Clinging Mire*: creatures it hits can't Disengage until their next turn"},"upgrade":{"name":"Swallowing Bog","limit":null,"text":"a creature restrained by its mud that fails 3 STR saves sinks and can't breathe","cell":"*Swallowing Bog*: a creature restrained by its mud that fails 3 STR saves sinks and can't breathe"}},{"id":"metal","name":"Metal","path":"Hybrid (Fire, Earth)","pathKind":"Hybrid","pathOf":["Fire","Earth"],"school":null,"status":"Bleed","statusName":"bleed","weakTo":"Water","movement":"30 ft","lair":"Shard storm: 1d8 bleed to anyone who moves more than 10 ft","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Shrapnel Scales","limit":null,"text":"when it takes a crit, everyone within 10 ft takes 2d6 bleed","cell":"*Shrapnel Scales*: when it takes a crit, everyone within 10 ft takes 2d6 bleed"},"upgrade":{"name":"Reforge","limit":null,"text":"it heals 50 HP by absorbing metal, putting 3 corrode stacks on a grabbed creature's armour","cell":"*Reforge*: it heals 50 HP by absorbing metal, putting 3 corrode stacks on a grabbed creature's armour"}},{"id":"comet","name":"Comet","path":"Sixth (Fire)","pathKind":"Sixth","pathOf":["Fire"],"school":null,"status":"Burn and stun (alternate)","statusName":"burn and stun","weakTo":"Earth","movement":"Fly 60 ft","lair":"Falling stars: 1d4 strikes a round at random points, 4d10 each","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Meteor Dive","limit":null,"text":"a dive from 60 ft or higher hits everyone in a 20 ft area for its bite damage and knocks them prone","cell":"*Meteor Dive*: a dive from 60 ft or higher hits everyone in a 20 ft area for its bite damage and knocks them prone"},"upgrade":{"name":"Starfall","limit":"once per combat","text":"1d6 meteors strike random points within 300 ft, 6d10 each","cell":"*Starfall* (once per combat): 1d6 meteors strike random points within 300 ft, 6d10 each"}},{"id":"the-deep","name":"The Deep","path":"Sixth (Water)","pathKind":"Sixth","pathOf":["Water"],"school":null,"status":"Crushed (restrained, 1d10 a turn)","statusName":"crushed","weakTo":"Air","movement":"Swim 80 ft","lair":"Crushing pressure: disadvantage on STR and Dodge","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Crushing Depths","limit":null,"text":"creatures within 20 ft move at half speed","cell":"*Crushing Depths*: creatures within 20 ft move at half speed"},"upgrade":{"name":"Abyssal Weight","limit":"once per combat","text":"a 60 ft area is crushed (restrained, 2d10 a turn) for 3 turns","cell":"*Abyssal Weight* (once per combat): a 60 ft area is crushed (restrained, 2d10 a turn) for 3 turns"}},{"id":"root","name":"Root","path":"Sixth (Earth)","pathKind":"Sixth","pathOf":["Earth"],"school":null,"status":"Entangled (restrained)","statusName":"entangled","weakTo":"Fire","movement":"Burrow 30 ft","lair":"Grasping roots, and it heals 20 HP a turn while touching soil","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Root Mending","limit":null,"text":"it heals 20 HP a turn while it touches soil","cell":"*Root Mending*: it heals 20 HP a turn while it touches soil"},"upgrade":{"name":"World Tree","limit":"once per combat","text":"its allies within 60 ft heal 40 HP and lose all statuses","cell":"*World Tree* (once per combat): its allies within 60 ft heal 40 HP and lose all statuses"}},{"id":"echo","name":"Echo","path":"Sixth (Air)","pathKind":"Sixth","pathOf":["Air"],"school":null,"status":"Deafened; at 2 stacks, the target's next spell rebounds on it","statusName":"deafened","weakTo":"Earth","movement":"Fly 40 ft","lair":"Echoing halls: every spell cast here repeats on a random target next round","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Mimic","limit":null,"text":"once a round, it repeats the last spell cast within 60 ft as its own","cell":"*Mimic*: once a round, it repeats the last spell cast within 60 ft as its own"},"upgrade":{"name":"Resonance","limit":null,"text":"when a spell targets it, roll 1d2, and on a 2 the spell rebounds onto its caster","cell":"*Resonance*: when a spell targets it, roll 1d2, and on a 2 the spell rebounds onto its caster"}},{"id":"light","name":"Light","path":"Magic: light","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"light","status":"Dazzled (disadvantage on attacks)","statusName":"dazzled","weakTo":"Dark","movement":"Fly 60 ft","lair":"Radiance: undead and dark-aligned creatures take 1d10 a turn","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Radiant Aura","limit":null,"text":"its allies within 30 ft heal 1d10 a turn, and dark-aligned enemies there take 1d10","cell":"*Radiant Aura*: its allies within 30 ft heal 1d10 a turn, and dark-aligned enemies there take 1d10"},"upgrade":{"name":"Judgement","limit":"as High Angel","text":null,"cell":"*Judgement* (as High Angel)"}},{"id":"dark","name":"Dark","path":"Magic: dark","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"dark","status":"Madness","statusName":"madness","weakTo":"Light","movement":"Fly 40 ft, and it can hide in any shadow","lair":"Corruption: all healing is halved","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Shadow Step","limit":null,"text":"once a round, it teleports up to 60 ft from one shadow to another","cell":"*Shadow Step*: once a round, it teleports up to 60 ft from one shadow to another"},"upgrade":{"name":"Eclipse","limit":"once per combat","text":"all light within a mile goes out for 3 rounds, and it has advantage while it lasts","cell":"*Eclipse* (once per combat): all light within a mile goes out for 3 rounds, and it has advantage while it lasts"}},{"id":"mind","name":"Mind","path":"Magic: mind","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"mind","status":"Charmed or confused (DM's pick)","statusName":"charmed or confused","weakTo":"Soul","movement":"Fly 30 ft (hover)","lair":"Illusions: the room shows a false layout, and a WIS save sees through it","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Mirror Image","limit":null,"text":"three illusory copies surround it. Roll 1d4 for each hit, and on 1–3 it destroys a copy instead","cell":"*Mirror Image*: three illusory copies surround it. Roll 1d4 for each hit, and on 1–3 it destroys a copy instead"},"upgrade":{"name":"Puppet","limit":"once per combat","text":"it takes control of one creature for a turn (two failed saves in a row, as normal)","cell":"*Puppet* (once per combat): it takes control of one creature for a turn (two failed saves in a row, as normal)"}},{"id":"life","name":"Life","path":"Magic: natural","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"natural","status":"Overgrowth (restrained)","statusName":"overgrowth","weakTo":"Death","movement":"30 ft","lair":"Bloom: its allies heal 1d10 a turn","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Overgrowth","limit":null,"text":"plants within 60 ft slow movement and entangle on a 1d2 roll of 2","cell":"*Overgrowth*: plants within 60 ft slow movement and entangle on a 1d2 roll of 2"},"upgrade":{"name":"Second Bloom","limit":"once a day","text":"when it first drops below half HP, it heals a quarter of its max HP","cell":"*Second Bloom* (once a day): when it first drops below half HP, it heals a quarter of its max HP"}},{"id":"death","name":"Death","path":"Magic: natural","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"natural","status":"Wither (max HP −1d10 until a long rest)","statusName":"wither","weakTo":"Life","movement":"30 ft","lair":"Nothing heals, and the fallen rise as zombies after 1 round","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Death's Door","limit":null,"text":"a creature it drops to 0 HP can't be healed until the combat ends","cell":"*Death's Door*: a creature it drops to 0 HP can't be healed until the combat ends"},"upgrade":{"name":"Unmaking","limit":"once per combat","text":"a creature below a quarter HP that fails two WIS saves in a row dies","cell":"*Unmaking* (once per combat): a creature below a quarter HP that fails two WIS saves in a row dies"}},{"id":"soul","name":"Soul","path":"Magic: natural","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"natural","status":"Soulshake (disadvantage on WIS; paralysed at 3 stacks)","statusName":"soulshake","weakTo":"Dark","movement":"Fly 40 ft (incorporeal)","lair":"The dead here manifest as ghosts","godTier":false,"signature":{"name":"Soul Siphon","limit":null,"text":"when any creature within 60 ft dies, it heals 50 HP and has advantage on its next attack","cell":"*Soul Siphon*: when any creature within 60 ft dies, it heals 50 HP and has advantage on its next attack"},"upgrade":{"name":"Ghostly Host","limit":"once per combat","text":"2d6 Shades rise and fight for it","cell":"*Ghostly Host* (once per combat): 2d6 Shades rise and fight for it"}},{"id":"creation","name":"Creation","path":"Magic: creation","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"creation","status":"Transmuted (a harmless object or animal for 1 turn)","statusName":"transmuted","weakTo":"Destruction","movement":"Fly 60 ft","lair":"Terrain reshapes each round as the DM wills","godTier":true,"signature":{"name":"Remake","limit":null,"text":"once a round, it creates a 20 ft wall, bridge or pit","cell":"*Remake*: once a round, it creates a 20 ft wall, bridge or pit"},"upgrade":{"name":"Reshape Reality","limit":"once per combat","text":"it ends one ongoing effect and reshapes all terrain within 300 ft","cell":"*Reshape Reality* (once per combat): it ends one ongoing effect and reshapes all terrain within 300 ft"}},{"id":"destruction","name":"Destruction","path":"Magic: destruction","pathKind":"Magic","pathOf":[],"school":"destruction","status":"Unmade (destroys a non-magical item or 2 Min hit)","statusName":"unmade","weakTo":"Creation","movement":"Fly 60 ft","lair":"Each round, something in the lair crumbles away","godTier":true,"signature":{"name":"Unravel","limit":null,"text":"its attacks ignore Min hit","cell":"*Unravel*: its attacks ignore Min hit"},"upgrade":{"name":"Annihilate","limit":"once per combat","text":"in a 30 ft sphere, anything on 100 HP or less is destroyed and everything else takes 20d10","cell":"*Annihilate* (once per combat): in a 30 ft sphere, anything on 100 HP or less is destroyed and everything else takes 20d10"}}]}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('disposition', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","rules":"Every dragon and elemental is either benevolent or malevolent, whatever its flavour. Disposition doesn't change the KR. It changes how the creature fights and what it wants.\n\n\nLight and dark lean towards their own side but aren't locked to it. A malevolent light creature is a zealot that burns anything it judges impure. A benevolent dark creature is a jailer that holds corruption in itself so it can't spread.\n\nA bound elemental follows its summoner's disposition, not its own, until it's freed.","rows":[{"aspect":"Wants","benevolent":"To guard something: a place, a people, a balance","malevolent":"To rule something, own it, or end it"},{"aspect":"Meeting it","benevolent":"Tests or bargains first, and won't start a fight with anyone who shows respect","malevolent":"Demands tribute, and treats trespassers as prey"},{"aspect":"In battle","benevolent":"Spares anyone who yields, and yields itself at a quarter HP if it's been beaten fairly","malevolent":"Targets the weakest first, and saves against its Frightful Presence are made at disadvantage"},{"aspect":"Its lair","benevolent":"Open to those it trusts, with its lair effect sparing its allies","malevolent":"Trapped and guarded by thralls or lesser creatures of its flavour"},{"aspect":"Reward","benevolent":"*Boon*: it can grant a temporary flavour-themed feat to those it favours","malevolent":"*Hoard*: an extra 1d4 legendary-tier items in its lair"},{"aspect":"When it loses","benevolent":"Grants passage, knowledge or its blessing","malevolent":"Flees at a quarter HP to plot revenge, which makes a good recurring villain"}],"options":["Benevolent","Malevolent"]}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('encounters', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","title":"Encounter tables for Pemmaroth","intro":"Use these suggestions for random encounters, or as a menu when planning a session. Pick a column by the party's combined level, then mix roles from the same cell.","bands":[{"label":"KR 1–5","min":1,"max":5},{"label":"KR 6–15","min":6,"max":15},{"label":"KR 16–35","min":16,"max":35},{"label":"KR 36–80","min":36,"max":80},{"label":"KR 81+","min":81,"max":null}],"regions":[{"name":"Pherontia, green north","cells":[["Wolf pack","Wild Boar","Bandits","Brown Bear","Sprite","Giant Owl"],["Dire Wolf","Griffin","Spriggan","Witch Hunter","Unicorn","Kelpie"],["Werebear","Hag","Wild Hunt Rider","Troll","Fey Knight"],["Oak Warden","Stone Giant","Adult Root or Life Elemental","Roc"],["Fey Monarch","Elder Grove","Elder Life Dragon"]]},{"name":"Pherontia, dark south","cells":[["Zombies","Skeletons","Giant Spider","Ghoul","Hive Warriors","Bat Swarm"],["Vampire Thrall","Ghost","Wight","Shade","Mantis Stalker","Bone Knight"],["Banshee","Headless Rider","Necromancer","Plague Lord","Hive Queen"],["Vampire","Fallen Knight","Lich","Wasp Empress","Bone Colossus"],["Elder Vampire","Dracolich","Archfiend"]]},{"name":"The worm desert","cells":[["Giant Scorpion","Hyenas","Giant Vulture","Giant Centipede","Bandits"],["Carrion Locust Swarm","Ghoul pack","Assassin","Dust Moth swarm"],["Mummy","Basilisk","Juvenile Sand Dragon","Juvenile Sand Elemental"],["Sandworm","Worm Matriarch (Alpha)","Colossal Centipede","Adult Sand Dragon"],["Elder Sand Dragon","Ancient Sand Elemental"]]},{"name":"Coasts and open sea","cells":[["Reef Shark","Giant Crab","Merrow","Corsairs","Jellyfish Bloom","Giant Eel"],["Giant Octopus","Orca pod","Pirate Captain","Kelpie","Harpy"],["Sea Hag","Ghost Ship","Juvenile Water or Deep Dragon"],["Sea Serpent","Ancient Shark","Abyssal Squid"],["Storm Giant","Island Tortoise","Trench Titan"]]},{"name":"Caves, ruins and the deep","cells":[["Rat Swarm","Ooze","False Chest","Animated Armour","Crawling Claw"],["Cave Bear","Mind Leech","Cave Lurker","Gargoyle","Flesh Golem"],["Gloomeye","Stone Golem","Whispering Prophet","Fungal Colossus"],["Tunnel Horror","Iron Golem","The Many-Mouthed"],["Star Maw","The Dreaming Thing","Colossus"]]}]}$bx$::jsonb)
  on conflict (key) do update set data = excluded.data, updated_at = now();

insert into public.bestiary (key, data) values ('rules', $bx${"source":"Bestiary: Volume I (Nov 17, 2026)","title":"Bestiary: Volume I","sections":[{"id":"using","title":"Using this bestiary","md":"Every creature has a **Kill Rating (KR)**: the combined adventurer level needed to kill it. Add up the party's levels, counting each level 0 character as ½, and compare the total with the KR.\n\n- **Ratings add up.** Three wolves are KR 3. A bandit captain with four bandits is KR 9.\n- **Party total equal to the KR** means a fair fight that can still go wrong. At about half the KR, expect deaths. At double, it's a comfortable win.\n- **Terrain, surprise and numbers** shift the real difficulty, so adjust on the day.\n\n### Reading a stat block\n\n- **HP**: hit points. **Defence** and **Min hit** work exactly as they do for player armour. A Min hit of 0 means any damage counts.\n- **Stats**: the six base stats, roll-under (lower is better). A dash means the creature doesn't have that stat.\n- **Combat**: Melee, Ranged, Dodge, Disengage and Casting. Any combat stat the creature doesn't use is left out.\n- **Status dice**: \"+2d2 bleed\" means you roll 2d2 alongside the damage, and each 2 applies one stack or one instance of that status.\n- **Harvest**: what can be taken from the body, for pricing in the price tool.\n\n### Shared rules\n\n- **Swarm**: single-target attacks deal half damage to it, and area attacks deal double. It can share other creatures' spaces and squeeze through any gap its smallest member could. Below half HP its damage is halved.\n- **Undead**: immune to poison, bleed and disease. It doesn't breathe, eat or sleep. Light-school magic deals double damage to it.\n- **Incorporeal**: non-magical weapons deal half damage. It passes through walls and creatures, but can't end its turn inside a solid object.\n- **Construct**: immune to poison, bleed, disease, fear and charm. It never checks morale.\n- **Mindless**: undead and constructs marked mindless can't be reasoned with, bluffed or frightened.\n- **Morale**: a beast flees at a quarter HP unless it's cornered or guarding young. Humanoids make a WIS save when their leader falls or half their side is down, and flee on a fail."},{"id":"running","title":"Running monsters","md":"These rules sit on top of every stat block and keep fights fair at every KR.\n\n### Actions and attacks\n\n- On its turn, a creature takes one action and makes **one** attack from its Attacks line. If the line says **Multiattack**, it makes every attack listed there as that one action.\n- A creature with *Tempo* gets extra actions at the end of the round. An extra action can be a move, one single attack or a recharge ability, but never a Multiattack.\n- A recharge ability (\"3-turn recharge\") is ready again after that many of the creature's own turns.\n- **Tells**: every big ability is signalled the turn before it happens, as written in the creature's Tactics line. That gives players a chance to spread out, take cover or interrupt it.\n\n### Reading the new lines\n\n- **Role** is how it fights. *Brute*: hits hard and soaks damage. *Soldier*: holds a line. *Skirmisher*: fast and mobile. *Artillery*: fights at range. *Controller*: disables and repositions. *Leader*: makes its allies better. *Lurker*: ambushes. *Swarm*, *Minion* and *Hazard* are what they sound like. *Solo*: built to fight a whole party alone. *Set piece*: the encounter is about an objective, not killing it.\n- **Wants** is what it would accept instead of a fight. **Tactics** is how to run it. *Tell* is what players see before its big move. *Exploit* is the weakness clever players can find.\n\n### Monster Min hit\n\n- A creature's Min hit only applies to weapon hits. Spells, status damage and area effects always count.\n\n### Solo creatures\n\n- A creature with the Solo role gets **Defiant 1**: once per combat, it shrugs off a status as it lands. It also gets one **reaction attack** per round, against a creature that hits it. At KR 50 and above it gets Defiant 2.\n\n### Effects that end a fight\n\n- Anything that would take a character out of the fight in one go needs **two failed saves on consecutive turns**. That covers turning to stone, possession, being controlled, a long charm and instant death. The first fail gives a warning state (restrained, dazed or slowed), and the second applies the full effect.\n\n### Status effects\n\nEach 2 on the status dice applies one stack. *Hard control* means stun, paralysis, sleep, frozen solid and petrification. When a hard control ends, the creature can't be hard-controlled again until the end of its next turn.\n\n| Status | Per stack | Max | How it ends |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Burn | 1d6 fire at the start of its turn | None | Loses 1 stack a turn. Water, or an action to smother it, clears all |\n| Bleed | 1d4 at the start of its turn | None | Loses 1 stack a turn. Any healing clears all |\n| Poison | 1 damage at the start of its turn, and −1 to all rolls | −5 to rolls | A STR save at the end of each turn removes 1 stack. Clears after combat |\n| Disease | One step towards sickness. At 3 stacks it catches the disease | 3 | Loses 1 stack per long rest, or with medicine |\n| Madness | At the start of its turn, roll a d20. If the roll is equal to or under its stacks, it acts randomly | 10 | Loses 1 stack per long rest, or with a tier 3 cleansing |\n| Wither | −1d10 max HP | None | Long rest |\n| Corrode | −1 armour Min hit | None | Repair |\n| Freeze | −10 ft speed. At 3 stacks it's frozen solid (hard control) for 1 turn, then clears | 3 | Fire clears all |\n| Stun, paralysis | 1 turn | 2 turns | Hard control |\n| Sleep | Asleep 1 turn | 2 turns | Hard control. Damage wakes it |\n| Blinded, dazzled, deafened, disorientated | 1 turn. Dazzled means disadvantage on attacks | 3 turns | Ends when the duration runs out |\n| Charmed, frightened, confused | 1 turn | 3 turns | A WIS save at the end of each turn ends it |\n| Prone, stagger | Knocked down, or loses its reaction | 1 | Standing up costs half its movement |\n| Knockback | 10 ft | None | Instant |\n| Restrained, grabbed, entangled, crushed | No stacks | 1 | A STR save to escape |\n\n### Building and checking a monster\n\nThis is the budget every stat block is tuned to. It's based on your players' numbers. Level 0 adventurers have about 15–35 HP, stats around 11 and hit for 1d6–1d8. Level 11 adventurers have 28–55 HP plus up to 75 armour temp HP, Melee 5–14 and Dodge 10–16, and hit for 1d20 to 1d50+10.\n\n| KR | HP | Melee / Ranged | Dodge | Damage per round | Min hit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ½–1 | 5–14 | 9 | 14 | 3–5 | 0 |\n| 2–3 | 14–35 | 9–8 | 14 | 6–9 | 0–2 |\n| 4–6 | 30–60 | 8 | 14 | 9–13 | 0–3 |\n| 8–14 | 60–130 | 7 | 13 | 14–21 | 2–4 |\n| 15–24 | 100–200 | 6 | 13 | 22–30 | 3–5 |\n| 25–45 | 200–380 | 5 | 12 | 30–45 | 4–7 |\n| 50–90 | 380–800 | 4 | 12 | 45–80 | 6–9 |\n| 100–200 | 900–2,000 | 3 | 11 | 80–145 | 9–12 |\n| 225–600 | 2,200–6,000 | 3 | 10 | 150–350 | 11–14 |\n\n- **Dodge by role**: Brute +3, Huge another +2 (to a maximum of 20), Skirmisher −2, Lurker −1, and Tiny or evasive fliers −4 (never below 8).\n- **Damage per round** counts every action it gets in a round, including Tempo. Melee and Ranged never go below 3. Set pieces ignore the budget.\n\n### Harvest values\n\n| Part | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Common part: pelt, hide, fangs, meat, chitin, feathers | KR × 10 silver |\n| Reagent: venom, blood, gland, dust, essence, ichor, spores | KR × 50 silver |\n| Legendary core: anything called a heartscale, core or heart, from KR 100+ | KR × 1 gold |\n| God-tier core: from a Primordial, Archfiend, Colossus, Titan or similar | KR × 5 gold |\n\nCoin in a stat block is what the creature carries, on top of its harvest. Run every value through your price tool for settlement size, supply and reputation."},{"id":"alpha","title":"The Alpha template","md":"Any creature in this book can be an **Alpha**, except a Primordial. An Alpha is the undiluted, oversized version that leads its kind, the way the Prime races relate to the playable races. Apply these changes to the creature's stat block:\n\n- **KR ×1.5**, rounded up. **HP ×1.5**. **Defence +1**, **Min hit +2**.\n- Every base stat and combat stat improves by 1, to a minimum of 1.\n- Every attack adds one more of its damage die, so a 2d8 bite becomes 3d8. Every status roll gets +1d2.\n- It has **one exaggerated physical divergence** and **one new signature trait**.\n- An Alpha dragon or elemental sits between two tiers. An Alpha Adult Dragon is KR 120.\n- Humanoids don't get Alphas. Use the race's Prime version instead.\n\n| Alpha | KR | Divergence | Signature trait |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Alpha Wolf | 2 | Twice the size, with a silver-white mane | *Pack Leader*: every wolf within 60 ft has Pack Hunter even when it's alone. If the Alpha dies, the pack flees. |\n| Rat King | 2 | A knot of rats fused at the tails, moving as one | *Plague Tide*: anyone who touches a creature it has infected makes the disease save too. |\n| Ossuary Champion | 2 | An eight-foot skeleton with a second pair of arms | *Four Arms*: it makes two extra weapon attacks. |\n| Abomination | 2 | Several corpses stitched into one hulk | *Many Mouths*: it Bites every creature it's grabbing. |\n| Alpha Bear | 5 | Shoulders like a hill, with bone plates under the fur | *Unstoppable*: it can't be knocked prone, grabbed or pushed. |\n| Brood Mother | 6 | A bloated body crawling with young | *Brood* (once per combat): it releases a swarm of spiderlings. Use Rat Swarm stats with poison instead of disease. |\n| Ghast | 6 | Jaw unhinged, with a battlefield stench | *Stench*: creatures that start their turn within 10 ft make a strength save or are poisoned. |\n| Ogre Warlord | 12 | Tusked, scarred and plated in looted armour | *Bully*: allies within 30 ft have advantage on attacks against prone targets. |\n| Alpha Troll | 30 | Two heads and stone-grey hide | *Twin Heads*: two Bites, and it only stops regenerating if it took fire or acid damage twice since its last turn. |\n| Hill Giant Chief | 42 | Thirty feet tall, wearing a boulder as a crown | *Earthshaker*: its Stomp hits everyone within 20 ft. |\n| Worm Matriarch | 60 | Three hundred feet long, with a cavern for a mouth | *Undertow*: each round, the sand within 100 ft drags everyone 10 ft towards it. |\n| Alpha Adult Dragon | 120 | A second pair of horns and a crest of crystal scales | *Twin Breath*: its breath recharges in 2 turns and can split into two cones. |"},{"id":"templates","title":"Group, Minion and Boss templates","md":"### Group\n\nA group of creatures gets more actions than their KRs add up to. After adding up the KRs of creatures that act separately, multiply the total:\n\n- 3–6 creatures: ×1.25\n- 7–12 creatures: ×1.5\n- 13 or more: ×2\n\nMinions don't count towards group size. Examples: four wolves are KR 4 × 1.25 = 5. A Bandit Captain with four Bandits is KR 9 × 1.25 = 11.\n\n### Minion\n\nAny creature of KR 8 or lower can be run as a minion, for hordes, armies or a necromancer's dead.\n\n- **KR ÷5**, so five minion wolves are KR 1.\n- **1 HP.** Any hit that deals damage kills it, but it still gets its Dodge roll.\n- Its attacks deal their average damage with no roll, and at most +1d2 status. It has no recharge abilities and no Tempo.\n\n### Boss\n\nUse this for a creature that carries a whole fight on its own.\n\n- **KR ×2, HP ×2.** It counts as Solo, with Defiant 2, or Defiant 3 at KR 50+.\n- **Boss Tempo**: one extra action at the end of each round, on top of any Tempo it already has.\n- **Phases**: at 66% and 33% HP it clears all its statuses and recharges one ability. Then pick one: the arena changes (collapse, flood, fire or darkness); it gains a new attack; it calls allies worth up to 10% of its KR; or it changes tactics completely (takes to the air, falls back to a second room, or turns on its own minions).\n- **Lair actions**: in its lair, at the top of each round, it uses one lair effect. Use its flavour's lair effect, or one from its Tactics line.\n- It stacks with the Alpha template. Apply Alpha first, then Boss."},{"id":"flavours","title":"Flavours","md":"Pick one flavour for any dragon or elemental. The status is what each 2 on its status dice applies. It takes double damage from the flavour in \"Weak to\", and it's immune to its own. Creation and Destruction are god-tier, so they only exist at Ancient and Primordial.\n\n| Flavour | Path | Status | Weak to | Elemental movement | Lair effect |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Fire | Element | Burn | Water | 50 ft | Ground smoulders: 1d10 burn to anyone ending a turn on it |\n| Water | Element | Knockback 10 ft | Cold | Swim 60 ft | Waist-deep water: half speed unless swimming |\n| Earth | Element | Stun | Water | Burrow 30 ft | Tremors: STR save each round or prone |\n| Air | Element | Disorientate | Earth | Fly 80 ft (hover) | Gale: disadvantage on ranged attacks, and fliers make a STR save or are blown 20 ft |\n| Smoke | Hybrid (Fire, Air) | Choking (poisoned) | Water | Fly 50 ft | Thick haze: can't see beyond 10 ft |\n| Steam | Hybrid (Fire, Water) | Scald (burn, ignores Min hit) | Cold | Fly 40 ft | Scalding fog: 1d6 burn a turn, can't see beyond 20 ft |\n| Cold | Hybrid (Air, Water) | Freeze | Fire | Ice-glide 50 ft | Ice: Dodge roll or prone when you move more than half speed |\n| Sand | Hybrid (Air, Earth) | Blinded | Water | Burrow 40 ft | Sandstorm and sinking sand: STR save or restrained |\n| Mud | Hybrid (Water, Earth) | Slowed | Fire | Burrow 20 ft, swim 30 ft | Sucking mud: half speed, and no Disengage |\n| Metal | Hybrid (Fire, Earth) | Bleed | Water | 30 ft | Shard storm: 1d8 bleed to anyone who moves more than 10 ft |\n| Comet | Sixth (Fire) | Burn and stun (alternate) | Earth | Fly 60 ft | Falling stars: 1d4 strikes a round at random points, 4d10 each |\n| The Deep | Sixth (Water) | Crushed (restrained, 1d10 a turn) | Air | Swim 80 ft | Crushing pressure: disadvantage on STR and Dodge |\n| Root | Sixth (Earth) | Entangled (restrained) | Fire | Burrow 30 ft | Grasping roots, and it heals 20 HP a turn while touching soil |\n| Echo | Sixth (Air) | Deafened; at 2 stacks, the target's next spell rebounds on it | Earth | Fly 40 ft | Echoing halls: every spell cast here repeats on a random target next round |\n| Light | Magic: light | Dazzled (disadvantage on attacks) | Dark | Fly 60 ft | Radiance: undead and dark-aligned creatures take 1d10 a turn |\n| Dark | Magic: dark | Madness | Light | Fly 40 ft, and it can hide in any shadow | Corruption: all healing is halved |\n| Mind | Magic: mind | Charmed or confused (DM's pick) | Soul | Fly 30 ft (hover) | Illusions: the room shows a false layout, and a WIS save sees through it |\n| Life | Magic: natural | Overgrowth (restrained) | Death | 30 ft | Bloom: its allies heal 1d10 a turn |\n| Death | Magic: natural | Wither (max HP −1d10 until a long rest) | Life | 30 ft | Nothing heals, and the fallen rise as zombies after 1 round |\n| Soul | Magic: natural | Soulshake (disadvantage on WIS; paralysed at 3 stacks) | Dark | Fly 40 ft (incorporeal) | The dead here manifest as ghosts |\n| Creation | Magic: creation | Transmuted (a harmless object or animal for 1 turn) | Destruction | Fly 60 ft | Terrain reshapes each round as the DM wills |\n| Destruction | Magic: destruction | Unmade (destroys a non-magical item or 2 Min hit) | Creation | Fly 60 ft | Each round, something in the lair crumbles away |\n\n### Signature moves\n\nEvery dragon and elemental gets its flavour's signature move from Adult upwards, and the upgrade from Ancient upwards. Creation and Destruction start at Ancient, so they get the first move there and the upgrade at Primordial.\n\n| Flavour | Signature move (Adult+) | Upgrade (Ancient+) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Fire | *Inferno Trail*: its flight leaves a 10 ft-wide trail of fire for a round, 2d6 burn to anyone crossing it | The trail becomes a 30 ft wall that lasts 3 rounds, 4d6 burn |\n| Water | *Undertow*: once a round, a creature that moves within 20 ft makes a STR save or is pulled 10 ft towards it | *Tidal Prison*: one creature is sealed in a sphere of water (restrained, can't breathe) until it passes a STR save or deals 30 damage to it |\n| Earth | *Tremor Step*: when it lands or stomps, everyone within 20 ft makes a Dodge roll or is knocked prone | *Mountain's Hide*: once per combat, its Min hit rises by 5 for 2 rounds |\n| Air | *Slipstream*: it can Disengage for free every turn, and ranged attacks against it have disadvantage | *Cyclone*: a 30 ft whirlwind it steers lifts creatures and flings them 30 ft |\n| Smoke | *Smokescreen*: as a reaction to being targeted, it becomes hidden in smoke until its next turn | *Choking Pall*: its smoke is poisonous, +2d2 poison a turn inside it |\n| Steam | *Scalding Hiss*: any creature that hits it in melee takes 1d10 burn | *Pressure Burst* (once per combat): it explodes in steam, 8d10 to everything within 60 ft, pushing it all 20 ft away |\n| Cold | *Frozen Ground*: the ground within 30 ft of it is always ice | *Shatter*: creatures that are frozen solid take double damage from its attacks |\n| Sand | *Sandswim*: it moves through sand at full speed and erupts to attack with advantage | *Hourglass* (once per combat): everything within 60 ft becomes sinking sand |\n| Mud | *Clinging Mire*: creatures it hits can't Disengage until their next turn | *Swallowing Bog*: a creature restrained by its mud that fails 3 STR saves sinks and can't breathe |\n| Metal | *Shrapnel Scales*: when it takes a crit, everyone within 10 ft takes 2d6 bleed | *Reforge*: it heals 50 HP by absorbing metal, putting 3 corrode stacks on a grabbed creature's armour |\n| Comet | *Meteor Dive*: a dive from 60 ft or higher hits everyone in a 20 ft area for its bite damage and knocks them prone | *Starfall* (once per combat): 1d6 meteors strike random points within 300 ft, 6d10 each |\n| The Deep | *Crushing Depths*: creatures within 20 ft move at half speed | *Abyssal Weight* (once per combat): a 60 ft area is crushed (restrained, 2d10 a turn) for 3 turns |\n| Root | *Root Mending*: it heals 20 HP a turn while it touches soil | *World Tree* (once per combat): its allies within 60 ft heal 40 HP and lose all statuses |\n| Echo | *Mimic*: once a round, it repeats the last spell cast within 60 ft as its own | *Resonance*: when a spell targets it, roll 1d2, and on a 2 the spell rebounds onto its caster |\n| Light | *Radiant Aura*: its allies within 30 ft heal 1d10 a turn, and dark-aligned enemies there take 1d10 | *Judgement* (as High Angel) |\n| Dark | *Shadow Step*: once a round, it teleports up to 60 ft from one shadow to another | *Eclipse* (once per combat): all light within a mile goes out for 3 rounds, and it has advantage while it lasts |\n| Mind | *Mirror Image*: three illusory copies surround it. Roll 1d4 for each hit, and on 1–3 it destroys a copy instead | *Puppet* (once per combat): it takes control of one creature for a turn (two failed saves in a row, as normal) |\n| Life | *Overgrowth*: plants within 60 ft slow movement and entangle on a 1d2 roll of 2 | *Second Bloom* (once a day): when it first drops below half HP, it heals a quarter of its max HP |\n| Death | *Death's Door*: a creature it drops to 0 HP can't be healed until the combat ends | *Unmaking* (once per combat): a creature below a quarter HP that fails two WIS saves in a row dies |\n| Soul | *Soul Siphon*: when any creature within 60 ft dies, it heals 50 HP and has advantage on its next attack | *Ghostly Host* (once per combat): 2d6 Shades rise and fight for it |\n| Creation | *Remake*: once a round, it creates a 20 ft wall, bridge or pit | *Reshape Reality* (once per combat): it ends one ongoing effect and reshapes all terrain within 300 ft |\n| Destruction | *Unravel*: its attacks ignore Min hit | *Annihilate* (once per combat): in a 30 ft sphere, anything on 100 HP or less is destroyed and everything else takes 20d10 |"},{"id":"disposition","title":"Disposition","md":"Every dragon and elemental is either benevolent or malevolent, whatever its flavour. Disposition doesn't change the KR. It changes how the creature fights and what it wants.\n\n|  | Benevolent | Malevolent |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Wants | To guard something: a place, a people, a balance | To rule something, own it, or end it |\n| Meeting it | Tests or bargains first, and won't start a fight with anyone who shows respect | Demands tribute, and treats trespassers as prey |\n| In battle | Spares anyone who yields, and yields itself at a quarter HP if it's been beaten fairly | Targets the weakest first, and saves against its Frightful Presence are made at disadvantage |\n| Its lair | Open to those it trusts, with its lair effect sparing its allies | Trapped and guarded by thralls or lesser creatures of its flavour |\n| Reward | *Boon*: it can grant a temporary flavour-themed feat to those it favours | *Hoard*: an extra 1d4 legendary-tier items in its lair |\n| When it loses | Grants passage, knowledge or its blessing | Flees at a quarter HP to plot revenge, which makes a good recurring villain |\n\nLight and dark lean towards their own side but aren't locked to it. A malevolent light creature is a zealot that burns anything it judges impure. A benevolent dark creature is a jailer that holds corruption in itself so it can't spread.\n\nA bound elemental follows its summoner's disposition, not its own, until it's freed."}],"categories":[{"id":"beasts","title":"Beasts","md":"These are natural animals, from KR 1 to 12. They fight to eat or to protect themselves, and most will flee before they die."},{"id":"undead","title":"Undead","md":"These are the risen dead, from KR 1 to 180. All of them follow the Undead shared rule, and some also follow Mindless or Incorporeal."},{"id":"humanoids","title":"Humanoids","md":"These are role templates, KR ½ to 45. The numbers already cover the role, so you can drop any playable race in, and add that race's two base traits if you want more flavour."},{"id":"monstrous","title":"Monstrous","md":"These are the classic monsters, from KR 2 to 150. Most of them have one trick the party has to work out to win."},{"id":"constructs","title":"Constructs","md":"These are magic-made guardians, from KR 1 to 200. All of them follow the Construct shared rule."},{"id":"fiends","title":"Fiends","md":"These are creatures of corruption from the lower planes, from KR 1 to 250.\n\n- **Fiend** (shared rule): it takes half damage from fire and poison, and double from light-school magic. Killing it away from its home plane only banishes it home, unless the killing blow is light magic."},{"id":"celestials","title":"Celestials","md":"These are servants and guardians from the upper planes, from KR 3 to 150. They're usually benevolent, but they can be zealots.\n\n- **Celestial** (shared rule): immune to disease and charm, and dark-school magic deals double damage to it. Killing it away from its home plane only sends it home, unless the killing blow is dark magic."},{"id":"fey","title":"Fey","md":"These are tricksters and courtiers of the wild places, from KR 1 to 120.\n\n- **Fey** (shared rule): advantage on saves against charm. Cold-iron weapons ignore its Defence and Min hit and deal double damage. A fey can't break its spoken word."},{"id":"aberrations","title":"Aberrations","md":"These are things from outside any plane the gods made, from KR 2 to 200.\n\n- **Aberration** (shared rule): immune to charm and fear, and mind-school spells cast on it are made at disadvantage. The first time a creature sees one, it makes a WIS save or takes +1d2 madness."},{"id":"plants","title":"Plants","md":"These are living plants that hunt, from KR 1 to 150.\n\n- **Plant** (shared rule): fire deals double damage to it, and it doesn't sleep. *Blindsight*: it senses everything within 30 ft through vibration."},{"id":"sea-creatures","title":"Sea creatures","md":"These are the dangers of the coasts and the open water between islands, from KR 2 to 250. Unless a creature is marked amphibious, it can't leave the water."},{"id":"insects","title":"Insects","md":"These are giant insects, from KR 1 to 70. Hive insects come in numbers, so build the encounter around the hive.\n\n- **Hive Mind** (shared rule for hive insects): every member shares senses with the rest of its hive within a mile, and none of them check morale while the queen lives."},{"id":"dragons","title":"Dragons","md":"A dragon is built from three parts: a **tier** stat block below, a **flavour** from the Flavours table, and a **disposition**. For example, an Adult Cold Dragon, benevolent, is KR 80.\n\nThe flavour sets the type of its breath, the status it inflicts, its immunity, its weakness and its lair. The stat block sets everything else. Every dragon is immune to its own flavour."},{"id":"elementals","title":"Elementals","md":"An elemental is its flavour given a body. You build one the same way as a dragon: tier, flavour and disposition. They hit harder up close and have more ways to control the battlefield than dragons, but less HP for their KR. Each one uses its flavour's movement from the Flavours table.\n\n- **Elemental** (shared rule): immune to poison, bleed, disease and its own flavour. It doesn't breathe, eat or sleep. *Formless*: it fits through any gap its flavour could pass through. *Merge*: it can hide inside a large mass of its flavour, such as a bonfire, a lake or a crowd's thoughts, and can't be targeted while it's there. *Bound*: if it was summoned, it obeys its summoner, and it goes free if the summoner dies. A banish spell of a tier equal to its tier number (Juvenile is 1, Primordial is 5) or higher sends it home."}],"named":"These 16 unique individuals are built from creatures in this book with the Alpha and Boss templates already applied. None is tied to a place, so put their lair wherever your campaign needs it. Each one has phases, lair actions, a hook and a named piece of loot.\n\n| Name | KR | Built from | Best as |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Old Tusker | 6 | Wild Boar, Alpha + Boss | A starting party's first legend |\n| Greymaw, the Pack-Mother | 10 | Dire Wolf, Boss | A hunt with a moral twist |\n| Skitter-Jack, King of the Sewers | 12 | Wererat, Boss | A city underworld villain |\n| Bramm the Toll-Keeper | 30 | Troll, Alpha | A bridge, a deal and a fight if you cheat |\n| Granny Nettlebone | 36 | Hag, Boss | A bargainer the party keeps coming back to |\n| The Weeping Bride | 40 | Banshee, Boss | A haunting with a mystery |\n| Varr Ironpenny, the Coin Warlord | 50 | Warlord, Boss | A mercenary army's general |\n| Lumen Vigil, the Unbending | 56 | Warden Angel, Boss | A good guardian blocking the party's path |\n| Sister Ashveil, the Plague Saint | 60 | Plague Lord, Boss | A villain who thinks she's merciful |\n| Rustmaw, the Furnace Bull | 60 | Bronze Bull, Alpha + Boss | A vault guardian |\n| The Briar Prince | 68 | Fey Knight, Boss | A court intrigue that ends in a duel |\n| Kragmaul, King of the Hill | 84 | Hill Giant, Alpha + Boss | A giant warlord |\n| Mother Brine, the Ship-Eater | 120 | Abyssal Squid, Alpha | A sea legend |\n| The Thousand-Eyed Choir | 120 | The Many-Mouthed, Boss | Cosmic horror under the city |\n| The Grey Abbot | 170 | Lich, Boss | A long-game mastermind |\n| Vhalrikka, the Last Ember | 240 | Adult Fire Dragon, Alpha + Boss | A campaign finale |","shared":[{"id":"swarm","name":"Swarm","text":"single-target attacks deal half damage to it, and area attacks deal double. It can share other creatures' spaces and squeeze through any gap its smallest member could. Below half HP its damage is halved.","from":"Shared rules"},{"id":"undead","name":"Undead","text":"immune to poison, bleed and disease. It doesn't breathe, eat or sleep. Light-school magic deals double damage to it.","from":"Shared rules"},{"id":"incorporeal","name":"Incorporeal","text":"non-magical weapons deal half damage. It passes through walls and creatures, but can't end its turn inside a solid object.","from":"Shared rules"},{"id":"construct","name":"Construct","text":"immune to poison, bleed, disease, fear and charm. It never checks morale.","from":"Shared rules"},{"id":"mindless","name":"Mindless","text":"undead and constructs marked mindless can't be reasoned with, bluffed or frightened.","from":"Shared rules"},{"id":"morale","name":"Morale","text":"a beast flees at a quarter HP unless it's cornered or guarding young. Humanoids make a WIS save when their leader falls or half their side is down, and flee on a fail.","from":"Shared rules"},{"id":"fiend","name":"Fiend","text":"it takes half damage from fire and poison, and double from light-school magic. Killing it away from its home plane only banishes it home, unless the killing blow is light magic.","from":"Fiends"},{"id":"celestial","name":"Celestial","text":"immune to disease and charm, and dark-school magic deals double damage to it. Killing it away from its home plane only sends it home, unless the killing blow is dark magic.","from":"Celestials"},{"id":"fey","name":"Fey","text":"advantage on saves against charm. Cold-iron weapons ignore its Defence and Min hit and deal double damage. A fey can't break its spoken word.","from":"Fey"},{"id":"aberration","name":"Aberration","text":"immune to charm and fear, and mind-school spells cast on it are made at disadvantage. The first time a creature sees one, it makes a WIS save or takes +1d2 madness.","from":"Aberrations"},{"id":"plant","name":"Plant","text":"fire deals double damage to it, and it doesn't sleep. *Blindsight*: it senses everything within 30 ft through vibration.","from":"Plants"},{"id":"hive-mind","name":"Hive Mind","text":"every member shares senses with the rest of its hive within a mile, and none of them check morale while the queen lives.","from":"Insects"},{"id":"elemental","name":"Elemental","text":"immune to poison, bleed, disease and its own flavour. It doesn't breathe, eat or sleep. *Formless*: it fits through any gap its flavour could pass through. *Merge*: it can hide inside a large mass of its flavour, such as a bonfire, a lake or a crowd's thoughts, and can't be targeted while it's there. *Bound*: if it was summoned, it obeys its summoner, and it goes free if the summoner dies. A banish spell of a tier equal to its tier number (Juvenile is 1, Primordial is 5) or higher sends it home.","from":"Elementals"}],"glossary":[{"id":"brute","term":"Brute","kind":"role","text":"hits hard and soaks damage.","match":["Brute"]},{"id":"soldier","term":"Soldier","kind":"role","text":"holds a line.","match":["Soldier"]},{"id":"skirmisher","term":"Skirmisher","kind":"role","text":"fast and mobile.","match":["Skirmisher"]},{"id":"artillery","term":"Artillery","kind":"role","text":"fights at range.","match":["Artillery"]},{"id":"controller","term":"Controller","kind":"role","text":"disables and repositions.","match":["Controller"]},{"id":"leader","term":"Leader","kind":"role","text":"makes its allies better.","match":["Leader"]},{"id":"lurker","term":"Lurker","kind":"role","text":"ambushes.","match":["Lurker"]},{"id":"solo","term":"Solo","kind":"role","text":"built to fight a whole party alone.","match":["Solo"]},{"id":"set-piece","term":"Set piece","kind":"role","text":"the encounter is about an objective, not killing it.","match":["Set piece"]},{"id":"multiattack","term":"Multiattack","kind":"rule","text":"On its turn, a creature takes one action and makes **one** attack from its Attacks line. If the line says **Multiattack**, it makes every attack listed there as that one action.","match":["Multiattack"]},{"id":"tempo","term":"Tempo","kind":"rule","text":"A creature with *Tempo* gets extra actions at the end of the round. An extra action can be a move, one single attack or a recharge ability, but never a Multiattack.","match":["Tempo"]},{"id":"recharge","term":"Recharge","kind":"rule","text":"A recharge ability (\"3-turn recharge\") is ready again after that many of the creature's own turns.","match":["recharge"]},{"id":"tell","term":"Tell","kind":"rule","text":"**Tells**: every big ability is signalled the turn before it happens, as written in the creature's Tactics line. That gives players a chance to spread out, take cover or interrupt it.","match":["Tell"]},{"id":"exploit","term":"Exploit","kind":"rule","text":"*Exploit* is the weakness clever players can find.","match":["Exploit"]},{"id":"wants","term":"Wants","kind":"rule","text":"**Wants** is what it would accept instead of a fight.","match":["Wants"]},{"id":"min-hit","term":"Min hit","kind":"rule","text":"A creature's Min hit only applies to weapon hits. Spells, status damage and area effects always count. **HP**: hit points. **Defence** and **Min hit** work exactly as they do for player armour. A Min hit of 0 means any damage counts.","match":["Min hit"]},{"id":"defence","term":"Defence","kind":"rule","text":"**HP**: hit points. **Defence** and **Min hit** work exactly as they do for player armour. A Min hit of 0 means any damage counts.","match":["Defence"]},{"id":"solo","term":"Solo","kind":"rule","text":"A creature with the Solo role gets **Defiant 1**: once per combat, it shrugs off a status as it lands. It also gets one **reaction attack** per round, against a creature that hits it. At KR 50 and above it gets Defiant 2.","match":["Solo","Defiant"]},{"id":"status-dice","term":"Status dice","kind":"rule","text":"**Status dice**: \"+2d2 bleed\" means you roll 2d2 alongside the damage, and each 2 applies one stack or one instance of that status.","match":["Status dice"]},{"id":"hard-control","term":"Hard control","kind":"rule","text":"Each 2 on the status dice applies one stack. *Hard control* means stun, paralysis, sleep, frozen solid and petrification. When a hard control ends, the creature can't be hard-controlled again until the end of its next turn.","match":["Hard control"]},{"id":"effects-that-end-a-fight","term":"Effects that end a fight","kind":"rule","text":"Anything that would take a character out of the fight in one go needs **two failed saves on consecutive turns**. That covers turning to stone, possession, being controlled, a long charm and instant death. The first fail gives a warning state (restrained, dazed or slowed), and the second applies the full effect.","match":["Effects that end a fight"]},{"id":"boss-tempo","term":"Boss Tempo","kind":"template","text":"**Boss Tempo**: one extra action at the end of each round, on top of any Tempo it already has.","match":["Boss Tempo"]}],"index":[{"kr":0.5,"name":"Commoner","type":"Humanoid"},{"kr":1,"name":"Wolf","type":"Beast"},{"kr":1,"name":"Rat Swarm","type":"Beast"},{"kr":1,"name":"Bat Swarm","type":"Beast"},{"kr":1,"name":"Viper","type":"Beast"},{"kr":1,"name":"Hyena","type":"Beast"},{"kr":1,"name":"Zombie","type":"Undead"},{"kr":1,"name":"Skeleton","type":"Undead"},{"kr":1,"name":"Crawling Claw","type":"Undead"},{"kr":1,"name":"Bandit","type":"Humanoid"},{"kr":1,"name":"Cultist","type":"Humanoid"},{"kr":1,"name":"Thug","type":"Humanoid"},{"kr":1,"name":"Homunculus","type":"Construct"},{"kr":1,"name":"Wretch","type":"Fiend"},{"kr":1,"name":"Sprite","type":"Fey"},{"kr":1,"name":"Screamroot","type":"Plant"},{"kr":1,"name":"Giant Tick","type":"Insect"},{"kr":2,"name":"Wild Boar","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Constrictor","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Reef Shark","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Giant Beetle","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Giant Centipede","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Giant Toad","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Panther","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Warhorse","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Giant Bat","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Giant Badger","type":"Beast"},{"kr":2,"name":"Plague Corpse","type":"Undead"},{"kr":2,"name":"Skeletal Hound","type":"Undead"},{"kr":2,"name":"Town Guard","type":"Humanoid"},{"kr":2,"name":"Corsair","type":"Humanoid"},{"kr":2,"name":"Scout","type":"Humanoid"},{"kr":2,"name":"O